3: Chapter 3: Two Pokemon\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What did father your say?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Dylan's expression, Ilene couldn't help but be curious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nothing much, just that he's still the same old joker."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan calmly folded the letter back into the envelope, making a light-hearted complaint about his father.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pfft~ Who talks about their dad like that? And what does 'joker' mean?" Ilene laughed softly, covering her mouth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just take it as a compliment," Dylan replied after a moment's thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"He prepared these two Pok\u233?mon for me. I wonder what they are; let's take a look."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan then curiously picked up the two Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sure!" Ilene was also very interested.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The two of them went to the backyard, and Dylan tossed out the two Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two beams of white light flashed, and two Pok\u233?mon appeared in front of them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233?mon on the left had a rather peculiar appearance, with ten tentacles hanging down like hair, covering its body. However, the tentacles in the front were short, allowing them to see its purple body.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a Mareanie.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The one on the right also had a strange appearance, resembling a shell-less snail with a pale purple body, green spots on its cheeks, and two antennae on its head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan was a bit surprised because this was a Goomy! Its final evolution is one of the Pseudo-Legendaries, Goodra or Hisuian Goodra.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Goodra, a Pseudo-Legendary!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, Pseudo-Legendary is just a common term among players. Officially, Pok\u233?mon like Goodra and Dragonite are referred to as "Late Bloomers."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Beep~ Goomy, Dragon-type, Soft Tissue Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Sap Sipper\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Dragon Breath, Water Gun, Absorb, Tackle, Counter (Egg Move)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: The weakest Dragon-type Pok\u233?mon. If its skin dries out, it won't be able to breathe, so it always stays in shady places."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Beep~ Mareanie, Poison/Water-type, Brutal Star Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Merciless\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Recover, Venoshock, Bite, Wide Guard, Poison Sting, Peck, Haze (Egg Move)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: It stabs its prey with its poison spike and then grabs it with its ten tentacles when it's weakened, delivering a fatal blow."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ilene took out her Pok\u233?dex and checked the information of the two Pok\u233?mon. Although she wasn't a trainer, she had still purchased a Pok\u233?dex as a useful tool.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, Goomy curiously looked around, while Mareanie remained quiet and seemed a bit shy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sprigatito took a few steps forward, its eyes full of curiosity as it looked at its new companions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They're both excellent."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan also finished checking the information on the two Pok\u233?mon. Well, it made sense\u8212?his father wouldn't have given him any subpar Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hello there, from today on, I'll be your trainer. Let's work well together."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan squatted down, speaking gently as he offered a Dragon-type and a Poison-type Pok\u233?block to the Pok\u233?mon. A mysterious wave of energy also emanated from him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Goo~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Goomy, clearly the more outgoing of the two, took a small bite of the Dragon-type Pok\u233?block, and its eyes lit up. It then happily called out to Dylan, its eyes squinting with joy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mareanie, on the other hand, remained quiet and shy, but it didn't reject Dylan's Pok\u233?block.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pok\u233?blocks are nutritious treats made from Berries that not only serve as food but are also delicious, making them a popular choice for Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
