Enhancing the strength of his Pok\u233?mon while obtaining a legendary one is quite motivating for Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once I train in nine regions and emerge, I'll punch Lance of the Kanto Elite Four, kick Leon of Galar, and easily suppress Steven and Wallace of Hoenn. No problem at all!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thinking even bigger, I'll call out that alpaca in the starting room, and if it dares to answer...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Forget it, that might be a bit too much. Let's focus on development first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hoo~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The next morning, Dylan opened his eyes and took a deep breath.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a whole night's effort, Floragato and the others had significantly leveled up, but the growth simulation world was not entirely gamified.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Traveling from Cerulean City to Vermilion City would take some time, with many wild Pok\u233?mon and trainers along the way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, Dylan wasn't in a hurry. The pace was already quite fast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After freshening up, Dylan went to the backyard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is for Floragato, this is for Glimmet, and this is for Mareanie\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan prepared breakfast for his Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Meow~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clefairy floated over, pointing at itself and making a pleasant sound.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I haven't forgotten you. This is especially for you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan picked up Clefairy, petted it several times, and then took out the prepared breakfast for it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Meow~ Meow~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clefairy was very satisfied.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Also, Clefairy can't fly, so be careful."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Meow\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clefairy happily enjoyed its breakfast, seemingly not paying much attention to Dylan's words.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan chuckled, sat on the picnic mat, and picked up his own breakfast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ilene, just in time. Come join me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan turned and saw Ilene in a white dress.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I've already eaten. You seem in good spirits today. Eh? Did Ekans evolve?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ilene smiled and elegantly sat beside Dylan, her eyes landing on the large, dark purple Arbok gulping down meat soup.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arbok is the evolved form of Ekans! Ilene recognized it, as Arbok is a dangerous wild Pok\u233?mon with a cruel nature, often involved in attacks each year.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arbok's appearance is also quite distinctive, being dark purple with black stripes and a creepy pattern on its chest resembling a large cobra.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, it worked hard." Dylan nodded with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Last night, Dylan had Ekans gain enough experience to evolve at level 25.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It looks very well developed. It must be over four meters long, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ilene took out her Pok\u233?dex and pointed it at Arbok.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The standard size of Arbok is around 3.5 meters, but Ilene estimated that Dylan's Arbok was over four meters long, indicating good development.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Ding~ Arbok, Poison-type, Cobra Pok\u233?mon\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Intimidate Moves: Thunder Fang, Ice Fang, Fire Fang, Crunch, Poison Fang, Screech, Glare, Sucker Punch, Haze\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: When it spreads its hood to intimidate opponents, it can emit a terrifying sound from its mouth to scare them.'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It looks so strong~!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ilene was surprised to see Arbok's stats. Its combat power had significantly increased compared to when it was Ekans! Ilene had personally seen Dylan capture Ekans, using the superior agility of his Sprigatito to defeat it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In just a few days, it had evolved into Arbok.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, you seem like a genius!" Ilene's eyes sparkled as she looked at Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although Ilene wasn't a trainer, she knew there were differences among trainers too! The talent of a trainer is intangible but very real.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two sixteen-year-olds starting at the same time with the same initial Pok\u233?mon could end up with vastly different strengths! One might become a champion dominating Kanto, while the other struggles to collect eight gym badges.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The world is never fair, that's the reality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To give a simpler example, with the same Weedle, one trainer might develop a Beedrill that can easily defeat another's Beedrill in a month. This is the real difference in trainer talent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan raising Ekans into Arbok in such a short time showed that he might have outstanding training talent! "Umm\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan pondered, not sure how to respond.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ilene, is there a possibility that while training, it just evolved?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
