46: Chapter 46: He\u8217?s Really So Sunshine-y\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan was unaware of what Leah and the others were thinking at the moment; his focus was entirely on the battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright, Red, let me see your final Pok\u233?mon."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan extended his hand with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red's red eyes were calm and focused. After a moment of contemplation, he threw out his starter Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Charizard!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roar~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a roar, a powerful Charizard flew above Red, its wings beating as it soared through the air without landing. (In "Pok\u233?mon Origins," Red's starter is Charmander.)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Looks like you're still cautious of Toxic Spikes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan chuckled lightly at this and wasn't too surprised. Charizard has flying abilities, but it's rare for Charizard to make an entrance in flight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red was evidently still wary of the Toxic Spikes. In the games, Toxic Spikes don't affect Poison, Steel, or Flying-type Pok\u233?mon, and they only take effect when Pok\u233?mon enter the field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that's just in the games. The fact that Paul's Drapion caused damage even when it threw Ash's Staraptor to the ground shows that, even for Flying-type Pok\u233?mon, touching the Toxic Spikes field upon landing still results in Toxic Spikes damage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, Toxic Spikes are really quite useful!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan had initially guessed that Red would use Charizard or Venusaur. In reality, Venusaur would be the best choice under normal circumstances.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Because Venusaur wouldn't be affected by Toxic Spikes. But Red is not one to give up easily. Even if victory seems unlikely, he'll still fight for it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Venusaur taking on three Poison-type Pok\u233?mon would be extremely difficult.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Charizard, go for it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Charizard come out, Ash was very excited. This was his brother's starter Pok\u233?mon, and it could definitely turn the tide!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come out, Charmander." Ash even released his own Charmander, wanting it to watch and learn from Charizard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Charmander, pay close attention. You'll evolve into something like this someday!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
