"Hmph~ Do you think you can escape?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, Lance noticed Archer and Proton's movements, but he wasn't too concerned about those two small fry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, go after them. It'll be good for you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance's eyes remained fixed on Giovanni and Beedrill as he spoke coldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He didn't care much for Archer and Proton, but Dylan was different. If Dylan could capture Archer and Proton, along with Ariana from before, the benefits he'd gain would be immense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seriously, even in front of Team Rocket's leader, Lance was still thinking about Dylan's future.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan was torn. He really wanted to stay and watch Lance and Giovanni's showdown! This was a rare, epic battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright, leave it to me, Lance," Dylan reluctantly agreed. He couldn't find a good excuse to stay.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before leaving, however, Dylan set up a camera drone, hoping it would survive to capture the fight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He hadn't gone far when he heard the sounds of a fierce battle. Clearly, Lance and Giovanni had started fighting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Using a hidden passage, Archer and Proton emerged onto a small street.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I hope the boss is okay," Proton said, worried.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't worry, let's just leave Celadon City for now. Move," Archer replied with a grim expression. This mission had been a complete failure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But he couldn't understand how Dylan had become so strong!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As they stepped out of the building and rounded a corner, Archer froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wearing a hat with clear, red eyes visible under the brim, dressed in a red jacket and blue jeans, stood Red!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red was also momentarily surprised to see Archer and Proton, but he quickly understood the situation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their disheveled appearance indicated they had escaped from Team Rocket's base.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two flashes of light appeared as Charizard and Pikachu took their places in front of Red.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red adjusted his hat, his expression unreadable. He had received a distress call from Leah earlier, but he had been too far from Celadon City at the time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
By the time he arrived, the League had already launched its attack, and Officer Jenny wouldn't allow him to assist. So, he had been patrolling the area when he stumbled upon the fleeing Archer and Proton.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Well, thank you, Mother Nature.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Isn't that the kid from the ship last time?" Proton whispered to Archer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Archer's eyelid twitched. Of course, he knew.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Relax! Archer, you're the top Executive of Team Rocket! This kid can't be as tough as Dylan. If we defeat him, we can escape. You can do it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Proton encouraged Archer, though he had no choice\u8212?his main Pok\u233?mon had all been defeated by Dylan. He couldn't exactly fistfight Charizard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Stop jinxing me, you idiot!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Archer suppressed the urge to smack Proton as he took out two Pok\u233? Balls. He had to focus on defeating this obstacle first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Red! Let's settle this!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's right, Red wasn't Dylan. There was no way he had gone easy on them back on the ship, right?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They had to win!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
