{\qc
96: Chapter 96: Dylan, You\u8217?ve Got the Wrong Person!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's expression was peculiar at the moment. If one had to describe it, it could be summed up as: awkward!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had only wanted to tease Blue a little by bringing up Red, but unexpectedly, Blue's stubborn side had kicked in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mr. Blue, gym challenges aren't something to be taken lightly. Besides, with your current strength, even if you didn't defeat me, you still qualify to receive the Rota Badge."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The implication: Stop messing around. Just take the badge and leave.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan carefully chose his words and took out a box containing the Rota Badge, offering it to Blue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although Blue had indeed lost this gym battle quite badly, especially since his team was swept by Darkrai, that didn't negate his overall strength, which was worthy of a badge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In fact, this was the third time Dylan had attempted to give out the Rota Badge. The first was to Red, the second to a diligent, bespectacled trainer who kept challenging him, and now the third time was to Blue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's criteria for awarding badges were quite high: strength (or potential), willpower, mindset, and command ability were all essential.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though Dylan always projected a sunny and polite image, deep down, he was proud and would only give his badge to someone who truly earned his approval.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To compete in the Indigo League, trainers only needed eight gym badges, and with Kanto's eight official gyms plus a number of smaller, unknown gyms, there were plenty of badges to earn without ever visiting the Rota Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, Dylan wasn't about to lower his standards. He aimed to make the Rota Gym's badge the most prestigious one of all!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What do you mean by this, Dylan?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But upon seeing the box with the Rota Badge, Blue's face immediately soured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't misunderstand, Mr. Blue. Since you're the grandson of Professor Oak, you should understand that gym leaders have more criteria for awarding badges than simply being defeated in battle."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"To be frank, with your strength, you're practically guaranteed to win the Indigo League, so you deserve this Dark Rota Badge."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan opened the box, showing Blue the badge inside.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blue's frown deepened as he stared at the Dark Rota Badge, which had been named by Dylan himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The badge was exquisitely crafted, emitting a faint glow. Blue, with his sharp eye, could tell at a glance that the material used to make it was far from ordinary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The badge even featured a small, stunning black diamond as decoration, making it look truly exceptional.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Rota Gym currently has two different types of badges, Dark and Poison, each corresponding to different attributes. Only those who have earned my approval for their mastery of these attributes will receive one."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wow, your gym is really over the top, isn't it? Even the badges have attributes? What, are you planning to make 18 different kinds of badges to match every type?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blue was stunned and momentarily speechless.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Normally, for challengers with strength like yours, Mr. Blue, I'd take the battle seriously."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This badge should rightfully be a testament to your victory, but\u8230? since I 'awakened,' I haven't given out a single badge. At this point, that doesn't seem quite right either."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan spoke with some helplessness. Though Officer Jenny understood Dylan's criteria for awarding badges\u8212?after all, each gym leader had different standards for their challengers\u8212?Jenny had still expressed concern. After all, Dylan hadn't given out a single badge in over a month, which was even stricter than Viridian or Cinnabar Gyms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing Dylan's honest words, Blue's expression softened significantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His pride was immense, and it was precisely because of that pride that, in the original story, he'd lost his cool after Red dethroned him as Champion so quickly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, I must seriously tell you, you've got the wrong person!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blue's handsome face now carried a rebellious expression, and his previously messy spiky hair was slicked back as he regained his confident, radiant self.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
