"You cheeky brat, putting on airs even with me," Itto laughed and scolded him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But I have to remind you, I've received word that lately, Lance hasn't been getting along with the Kanto League."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just last week, during the operation to suppress Team Rocket in Celadon City, which you participated in, the day after, there was a Kanto League meeting. It's said that Lance got into a conflict with the council members, and he even released his Dragonite during the meeting."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto clicked his tongue in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Senior Lance does have quite the temper," Dylan's eyes narrowed slightly upon hearing this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's mainly the council members. Those fools are incompetent, but they are arrogant, greedy, and self-righteous. They probably criticized Lance during the meeting, pushing him too far."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto was gleeful at their misfortune, having no fondness for the Kanto League council members, who had often used their positions to extort money from him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But just as he finished speaking, he noticed his son giving him a strange look.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's the matter?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You've got it wrong."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wrong? How so?" Itto was taken aback. Could his information be incorrect? No way, he had confirmed it with several people.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Senior Lance definitely didn't lose his temper," Dylan shook his head, speaking seriously to his father.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If those council members had really angered Senior Lance, they wouldn't have walked out of that meeting room."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan was certain that the Lance of this world was absolutely the same as the one in the Pok\u233?mon Adventures manga\u8212?perhaps not as extreme yet, but if truly pushed to the brink...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reenacting the events of the manga? Lance could absolutely do it. A few arrogant council members? Nothing a swipe from Dragonite couldn't handle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even in this world, Lance had certainly eliminated quite a few Team Rocket members behind the scenes. He wouldn't show mercy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto was shocked by this revelation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That... surely... couldn't happen, right?" Itto frowned. This wasn't something to joke about.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, Dad, it's entirely possible," Dylan's eyes flickered slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He suddenly realized why, after rescuing Proton and Archer, Giovanni had left that bold message at the Celadon Police Department.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the time, Dylan had found it strange, as it didn't seem like something Giovanni would typically do. But now, he understood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni had already seen Lance's increasingly obsessive and twisted nature. He was pushing him!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance, who was proud and fiercely protective of Pok\u233?mon and nature, would eventually be consumed by his extreme love! As long as Team Rocket existed, Lance would never be able to surface.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni was deliberately provoking Lance, trying to push the Dragon Master deeper into darkness!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When that time comes, Lance, who was once Kanto's Champion and protector, might become an even greater threat than Team Rocket\u8212?a nightmare for Kanto!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Whoa, now that's an exciting thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if Senior Lance really does turn evil, as a Gym Leader, would I have to step in?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That wouldn't feel right. Senior Lance has taken such good care of me as his junior.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan hesitated for a second before deciding he would have to step in. If his mentor lost his way, it was his duty as a junior to bring him back with Articuno!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Darn it, I really wish I had Kyurem right now!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
