101: Chapter 101: Dylan, She's Your Childhood Friend!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Champion-level Dragon-type Trainer!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing Zinnia's words, Ilene and Lillie were both very surprised. A Champion-level trainer is at the top of the ranks in any region. Such an opponent is undoubtedly extremely formidable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The news that Dylan and Zinnia would battle quickly spread through Meteor Village, attracting not only the elder but also many of the remaining Meteor villagers who came to watch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the open space in front of the village.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then I'll be the referee."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto stepped forward without hesitation. Unfortunately, Meteor Village was quite primitive and lacked scoreboards or similar facilities, but that wasn't a big issue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now the battle between Dylan and Zinnia begins!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The battle rules are 6 vs 6! Both sides can switch Pok\u233?mon, and the battle ends when one side's six Pok\u233?mon are all unable to continue. The other side wins!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The battle starts!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto waved a small flag and then stepped off the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Zinnia took out a Pok\u233? Ball, enlarging it and pointing it at Dylan, her face showing a bright and fearless smile, full of heroic spirit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Since Aster left, I have been honing myself and my Pok\u233?mon day by day, and I have finally become who I am now!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The fangs and claws of Dragons are their most powerful weapons! Can you withstand them?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing that Dylan remained unfazed, Zinnia threw the Pok\u233? Ball with force.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Goodra!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233? Ball opened, and a bipedal Dragon appeared before Zinnia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a tall and robust figure, mostly purple, with very smooth skin, a thick and massive tail, and a layer of slime on its body.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was Goodra, the final evolution of Goomy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Drip~ Goodra, Dragon-type, Dragon Pok\u233?mon\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Hydration\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Signature Moves: Draco Meteor, Muddy Water, Body Slam, Dragon Pulse, Rain Dance, Dragon Breath, Dragon Claw, Thunderbolt\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: This Pok\u233?mon is very affectionate toward people. It gets lonely when its trainer is not around and cries sticky tears.'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The first Pok\u233?mon was Goodra\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie, who wasn't a trainer herself, clicked her tongue in admiration as she read the Pok\u233?dex information on Goodra. Although she wasn't a trainer, she knew that being called a 'late-blooming Pok\u233?mon' was extremely rare and valuable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's really strong," Ilene said, her lips pressed together, her brows slightly furrowed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just from Goodra's aura, one could sense that its strength was likely very high.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This Goodra is probably at least level 65 or higher."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan carefully observed Goodra, pondering.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had a Goodra himself, but his Goodra was probably not as high a level as Zinnia's.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In that case, he would need to slightly adjust his strategy. Although he had Articuno as backup, Zinnia's strength was higher than anticipated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Incineroar, prepare for battle."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan threw out Incineroar's Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Incineroar landed, opening its arms and roaring fiercely at Goodra, showing a menacing pose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh~ Is this the evolved form of the Litten I sent?" Itto's eyes lit up as he took out his Pok\u233?dex to check Incineroar's information.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He nodded in satisfaction as he read, clearly proud of his son.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Incineroar?" Zinnia recalled Incineroar's type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
