{\qc
108: Chapter 108: Go Awaken Groudon and Kyogre!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan did not refuse Zinnia's request. Although he considered himself a selfish person, the tragic death of his childhood friend weighed heavily on him. Now that he knew the truth, helping out seemed reasonable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moreover, assisting Zinnia meant securing a future Champion-level ally. While it was uncertain if Zinnia could reach the pinnacle of the Champion class, with her talent and ability, she'd definitely be a formidable Champion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But Zinnia, this is a significant matter; you need to be well-prepared," Dylan reminded her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In Dylan's view, only the Devon Corporation posed a challenge among the three forces. The Celestic family and the Johto Pok\u233?mon Association weren't much of a problem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although the Celestic family had a long history of over 200 years and considerable wealth, much like the Silph Co., they lacked Champion-level strength. Even Team Rocket managed to infiltrate Silph Co. silently. With Zinnia's Champion-level power, wiping out the Celestic family wouldn't be too difficult.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, despite her hatred, Zinnia only wanted to target those involved in the "Rayquaza Capture Plan." If she went too far, the Pok\u233?mon League might hunt her down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Johto Pok\u233?mon Association held some power, especially with its ties to the Kanto League, but like Celestic, they lacked top-tier strength. As long as Zinnia avoided traps, she could handle them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The real problem was Devon Corporation. The tricky part was its heir, Steven. Devon's president, Joseph Stone, was directly involved in the plan. Since Steven was his son, dealing with Joseph meant confronting Steven.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could Zinnia take on Steven? Dylan thought it might be tough.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
