Though the Tree of Beginning viewed humans as 'viruses,' it was much kinder to Pok\u233?mon, and its defense mechanisms didn't target them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gao~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, the Alolan Vulpix were excited at the sight of the snow mountain, and the Alolan Ninetales looked at the children affectionately, giving a grateful cry to Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No need to thank me," Dylan nodded with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Blue, I've already got the team for our next battle. I hope you like the combination of Alolan Ninetales and Articuno."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Another day passed in the blink of an eye. There were quite a few challengers these past few days, though none of them were particularly impressive.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I wonder when Blue will challenge me for the second time. A strong challenger like that is interesting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though it's also fun to deal with the cute challengers, part of the enjoyment comes from the fact that Dylan was using a 'standard' lineup. Watching those challengers grit their teeth in frustration, their faces turning pale from the challenge, filled Dylan with a sense of satisfaction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They were feeling his 'love,' which was amusing. Otherwise, if it were just regular battles, Dylan might get bored.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It's no wonder most Gym Leaders in the original story had side jobs. If they didn't, and just spent all their time dealing with challengers, who wouldn't get tired of it? A side job helps keep life exciting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, the number of outstanding and powerful challengers who really impress is quite small. No wonder Volkner, the Sinnoh Gym Leader from Sunyshore City, got so burnt out. As a Gym Leader at an Elite Four level, facing weak challengers all the time must be incredibly boring.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'The handsome Dylan Gym Leader will be away for the next two days. Challengers, please return later to challenge the Gym...'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan hung the sign up again, satisfied, and slung his backpack over his shoulder.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan called out to Leah and Lillie.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Brother, are you sure this is okay? Can Gym Leaders really take time off?" Lillie asked, surprised as her image of Gym Leaders was reshaped once again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course. Your brother became a Gym Leader to enjoy life, not to be some corporate drone. Who works without any days off? No normal person would do that!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan replied with confidence, leaving Lillie unable to find a reason to refute him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it seemed there was really nothing to refute; Dylan was indeed a very responsible and good gym owner.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go, two beautiful ladies, I'll take you for a drive."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan tossed his backpack into the luxury car, took his place in the driver's seat, and signaled for Leah and Lillie to get in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~ I really am benefitting from the young master's generosity."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Leah, you're really cunning."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leah stretched her long legs and sat in the passenger seat, while Lillie pouted; she also wanted to sit in the passenger seat with Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a press of the accelerator, the car sped away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pallet Town\u8212?a legendary place for those who loved Pok\u233?mon in their past life.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The starting point of the first generation, and so it was in the anime, while in reality, Pallet Town was an ordinary rural town, but not so ordinary because the famous Professor Oak's research lab was located there.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The name Pallet symbolizes the pure white color of a journey's beginning, which is quite meaningful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And now, Dylan and the others had arrived at Pallet Town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pallet Town~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looking at the town scenery along the way, Leah's usually bright and lively eyes held a hint of complexity. She should have grown up healthily in this town and set out to become a trainer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But because of that incident, she lost her childhood, and after escaping from that organization, she found that her parents had already moved away from Pallet Town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Soon, the car stopped at the iconic large windmill research lab.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan parked the car and took Leah and Lillie to knock on the lab's door. In no time, a researcher in a white lab coat opened the door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unlike in the anime, Professor Oak's lab actually had some assistants.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
