"That kid Blue's talent far exceeds mine when I was young, but his personality is too proud. I'm really worried; he's had to suffer a loss at your place, so I really have to thank you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Oak said with a hearty laugh. He wanted to correct Blue's overly arrogant nature, but there was no way. He originally expected Blue to possibly lose to Red in a crucial battle, and he truly worried that the proud Blue wouldn't be able to handle the result.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now that another peer trainer had defeated Blue, Professor Oak sincerely believed this was a good thing for Blue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come, come, come, let's go into the research lab. Dylan, I know your purpose for coming; I happen to have taken them in a while ago."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Oak clapped his hands, leading Dylan and the others into the lab.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In fact, I've always wanted to find a suitable trainer for them. If it's you, Dylan, I think it should be fine."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Oak brought them to the guest room, then went to another room to retrieve two Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When the Pok\u233? Balls were opened by Professor Oak, two beams of white light flashed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pikachu?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eevee~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two adorable cries sounded as a Pikachu and an Eevee appeared on the table, curiously looking at Dylan and the others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
