133: Chapter 134: Frontier Brain!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time flew by, and half a month had already passed in the blink of an eye.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
During this time, Dylan's Dragon-type team had begun to take shape, and Rota Gym's roulette now boasted a new type\u8212?Dragon!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unsurprisingly, this addition gained significant popularity among challengers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, the Kanto Champion, Lance, is known for his Dragon-type Pok\u233?mon, and many people in Kanto hold a special fascination for Dragons.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, Kanto has very few native Dragon-type Pok\u233?mon, making it hard for many trainers to fulfill their desires.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With the new Dragon-type lineup at the Rota Gym, it became quite popular, as many people were eager to experience the power of Dragons firsthand!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Well, the Dragon-type team had only been available for three days, and those lucky enough to face it claimed Dylan's methods were utterly ruthless.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After battling him, they didn't want to engage in Pok\u233?mon battles again for a while.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Today was Friday, at Rota Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In one more week, I'll reach the Necrozma storyline." Dylan sat in the backyard, a smile slowly spreading across his face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes, his simulation in the Alola region was finally advancing to the Necrozma plot.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This also meant he was close to completing Alola's first storyline! He was about to get Necrozma!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Once I get Necrozma, I'll head to the Unova region."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's eyes flickered. If N could take Zekrom from Dragonspiral Tower, then I, Dylan, can surely take Reshiram!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan considered himself real enough\u8212?who in this world is more real than him?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If my authenticity can't awaken the White Dragon, then I'll just physically force it to. With Necrozma, I won't need to worry about such things."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan confirmed his plan. No matter what, he would head to Unova for Reshiram. Once he found it, things should go much smoother.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Brother~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's up, Lillie?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan looked toward Lillie, who was running toward him in a flowing white dress.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Someone's here to see you. He said his name is Carsey." Lillie's smile was pure and sweet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Carsey?" Dylan raised his brow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the guest room...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah~ I've heard so much about the famous Dylan! Now that I've seen you, you're just as impressive as they say\u8212?young, heroic, and full of potential!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The chubby, trendy man with curly hair and sunglasses enthusiastically shook Dylan's hand. Or rather, he was overly enthusiastic, with no sense of personal space.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You've taken down multiple high-ranking Rocket executives! Now, you're the hottest Gym Leader in Kanto! You've created various tactics and roulette challenges. My admiration for you is like a river, flowing endlessly, or\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carsey continued his excessive praise, possibly not even aware of what he was saying anymore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Behind Dylan, both Ilene and Lillie had peculiar expressions on their faces.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Stop, stop, any more praise and I'll blush. Carsey, just tell me\u8212?what do you need?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan interrupted with a laugh, gesturing for Carsey to sit down while he asked curiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~ Dylan, your popularity in Kanto is soaring! Super high!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carsey grinned, lowering his sunglasses slightly to give Dylan a thumbs-up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I personally admire you a lot\u8212?seriously amazing!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But have you ever heard of the Battle Frontier?" Carsey asked, changing the subject.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Battle Frontier?" Lillie and Selene were both surprised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Battle Frontier, also known as the Battle Zone, is a facility open only to elite trainers. It's similar to Gyms, but much more difficult to challenge," Dylan explained.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The trainers in charge of these facilities are incredibly strong."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's explanation was spot-on. The Battle Frontier is indeed harder than regular Gyms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In particular, the Battle Frontier in Kanto boasts top-tier trainers like Salon Maiden Anabel and Pyramid King Brandon. They are not opponents ordinary trainers can overcome.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before Caitlin became a Unova Elite Four member, she was also one of the Frontier Brains in the Sinnoh region, though her butler often battled in her place since she couldn't control her psychic powers back then.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~ Dylan, you're absolutely right." Carsey's grin widened, his tone full of pride.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Battle Frontier is a place for strong trainers, and if you defeat a Frontier Brain, you earn a 'Symbol,' a badge of honor!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carsey, who was responsible for recruiting strong trainers to serve as Frontier Brains, had every reason to be proud.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
