"It is. Some of the trainers in the Battle Frontier are extremely powerful," Dylan nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But I'm curious\u8212?why have you come to see me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan was puzzled. Carsey, who should be traveling the world recruiting strong trainers for the Battle Frontier, had shown up here.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could it be that he wanted Dylan to become a Frontier Brain?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~ Would you be interested in becoming a Frontier Brain, Dylan?" Carsey rubbed his hands together with a sleazy grin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ah, so that's what this was about.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Carsey, what makes you think I'd give up being a Gym Leader to become a Frontier Brain?" Dylan chuckled. He acknowledged that the Battle Frontier was prestigious, especially with trainers like Anabel and Brandon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the Battle Frontier was a privately-run facility, while Gym Leaders were backed by the Pok\u233?mon League, a much more secure position.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd have to be out of his mind to quit being a Gym Leader to become a Frontier Brain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't get me wrong, Dylan! That's not what I meant." Carsey quickly shook his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What I'm suggesting is that you continue being a Gym Leader while also taking on a part-time role as a Frontier Brain. What do you think?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan raised his brow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I can arrange for your Battle Facility to be scheduled later on. Given your strength, you definitely deserve it," Carsey said sincerely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You've got more to this plan, don't you?" Dylan glanced at Carsey. This guy didn't seem very serious, and he definitely had some tricks up his sleeve.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~ You're sharp, Dylan. Since you know about the Battle Frontier, you probably realize that challengers are handpicked elite trainers\u8212?either chosen by me or recommended by the Frontier Brains."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But we still don't have enough challengers," Carsey admitted, throwing up his hands helplessly. He wanted to maintain the Battle Frontier's high standards, which meant it was only open to top-tier trainers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, there weren't many trainers at that level, and it was even harder to find those willing to challenge the Frontier.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So, you think I could make recommendations?" Dylan asked, raising his brow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
