136: Chapter 137: That detestable fatty\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What a powerful Salamence, Dylan! You've trained it exceptionally well."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Brandon praised openly. Without a doubt, this was the strongest Salamence he had ever seen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a pseudo-legendary Pok\u233?mon, Salamence's bloodline advantage was already immense. Once fully trained, its power far surpassed that of many ordinary Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, for most lucky Trainers who obtain a Bagon, evolving it into a Salamence is no easy feat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The title of "late bloomer Pok\u233?mon" is not without merit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even after its evolution into Salamence, very few Trainers can bring out its full potential and strength.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's Salamence was unquestionably trained to near perfection, even stronger than Drake's Salamence. Brandon had never heard of such a powerful Salamence before today and hadn't expected that Dylan had secretly raised one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you for your kind words, senior," Dylan replied with a smile, then recalled his Salamence into its Pok\u233?ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Salamence cursed, it couldn't continue to battle without a huge risk.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since this wasn't a Gym battle, Dylan had the freedom to switch Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well then, Dylan, my second Pok\u233?mon is this one!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a moment of thought, Brandon decisively threw out his second Pok\u233?ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Solrock!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a flash of white light, a strange-looking Pok\u233?mon appeared, hovering before Brandon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its body was orange, with eight yellow rock spikes extending from its sides. Its front and back were adorned with patterns made of small yellow stones, and its large, crescent-shaped eyes gleamed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was Solrock, a Rock and Psychic-type Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Beep~ Solrock, Rock and Psychic-type, Meteorite Pok\u233?mon\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Levitate\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Explosion, Trick Room, Solar Beam, Stone Edge, Psychic, Morning Sun, Flare Blitz, Cosmic Power\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: Said to have fallen from space, Solrock silently floats through the air, emitting a bright light during battles.'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It looked just like a little sun. Quite fascinating.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie curiously observed the Solrock, its quiet aura and unique appearance truly living up to its name.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, this is quite a coincidence, Brandon, but I'm not targeting you intentionally," Dylan said as he enlarged the Pok\u233?ball in his hand and threw it out with a reverse flick.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dragapult, get ready for battle!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the Pok\u233?ball opened midair, a spectral dragon, part ghost and part tangible, descended and quietly faced Solrock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its head was triangular, with horns extending to the sides that housed four cannon-like holes. Its golden eyes gleamed eerily, and its long, thick tail became transparent at the end, exuding a chilling and menacing presence, in stark contrast to the fierce and brutal nature of Salamence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Brandon closely examined the unfamiliar dragon, his brows furrowing as a realization hit him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is that\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carsey gazed in astonishment at the eerie dragon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dragapult! A pseudo-legendary Dragon-type Pok\u233?mon from the Galar region."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Anabel's eyes lit up again with excitement\u8212?another pseudo-legendary dragon!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Beep~ Dragapult, Dragon and Ghost-type, Stealth Pok\u233?mon\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Clear Body\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Dragon Darts, Dragon Rush, Phantom Force, Dragon Dance, Hex, Sucker Punch, Quick Attack, Outrage\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
