This Dragapult looked incredibly powerful!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is Gym Leader Dylan really this strong? How did he acquire both Salamence and Dragapult?" Anabel couldn't help but blurt out, not really directing the question at anyone in particular.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan was a Gym Leader from Kanto, yet both Salamence and Dragapult were incredibly rare pseudo-legendary Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
How did a Kanto Gym Leader manage to get his hands on these two powerful dragons? If he had a pseudo-legendary, shouldn't it logically be Kanto's Dragonite or Tyranitar instead?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wait, does he also have a Dragonite? Anabel suddenly considered this possibility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?" Carsey was speechless. How was he supposed to know?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Bagon was a gift to Dylan from an old lady, while the Dreepy was a reward from Chairman Goodshow for capturing a Rocket Executive," Ilene answered in her pleasant voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"???"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Anabel and Carsey were even more shocked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Never mind who that old lady was, but a Dreepy as a reward for capturing a Rocket Executive? Well, capturing a high-ranking Rocket member was a significant achievement, so awarding a pseudo-legendary wasn't that far-fetched.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if they remembered correctly, the first time Dylan captured a Rocket Executive was in Celadon City, just under two months ago.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Dylan had already evolved the Dreepy into a Dragapult???\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
