148: Chapter 149: Merely an empty shell\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't be so afraid, Reshiram. You are the True Dragon God, after all, and Kyurem is just an ice dragon."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, no, no, Dylan, I don't think you understand."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan could almost imagine Reshiram shaking its head frantically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"At that time, because of differences in ideals, I and the black dragon separated from the body of the Original Dragon. We inherited the inner power of the dragon, but its shell was left behind, which eventually turned into Kyurem."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reshiram explained the origin of the Three Dragons of Unova to Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Do you understand what I mean, Dylan? At the root, both Zekrom and I are parts of Kyurem that were lost. It can capture me and the black dragon, then reintegrate us back into itself to restore the body it lost."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Being originally just a shell, Kyurem possesses power that surpasses mine and the black dragon's. Although we separated and took some of the power, a portion of the 'inner essence' still remains within Kyurem."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Its true power is far beyond what I can compare to now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reshiram spoke softly, revealing why both it and Zekrom preferred to stay hidden from Kyurem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't just because of the overwhelming difference in strength; the most terrifying thing was that Kyurem was a "hero waiting to fill its lost body with truth and ideals!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The consciousness of the Original Dragon of Unova had long since perished, splitting into three: Zekrom, Reshiram, and Kyurem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Kyurem was special! If any of the three dragons could return to their original form as the Original Dragon of Unova, only Kyurem had the potential to do so!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So, you're saying Kyurem is incredibly strong?" Dylan leaned on his hand, gazing at the massive gray dragon in the distance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, extremely strong!" Reshiram replied seriously. It seemed that its hero finally understood the gravity of the situation, which brought Reshiram some relief.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tsk~ That only makes it more appealing. Now, I really want to capture it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's eyes glinted with excitement. From Reshiram's words, he had grasped a crucial piece of information.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When the Original Dragon split, its shell still retained some of the 'inner essence'? In that case, this Kyurem could be just like the one in the movies!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"???" The white dragon was confused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't worry, Reshiram. Be brave. As your hero, I'll always be your strongest support!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan reassured the suddenly nervous white dragon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll have Necrozma ready to assist you at any time. If you can't handle it, we'll gang up and show 'truth' what's what!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Are you sure, Dylan?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reshiram was skeptical about the sincerity of Dylan's words, especially since fighting the ice dragon was\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course, I'm sure. You're my white dragon, after all. Do you think I'd just stand by and watch you get beaten up by an ice dragon?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then, Dylan, make sure Necrozma is on standby at all times, okay? Watch closely."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reshiram was still a little uneasy and kept reminding Dylan repeatedly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Relax, relax~ You can count on me." Dylan's eyelid twitched slightly. This white dragon was too much.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, Dylan looked towards Kyurem in the distance. His Rotom Pok\u233?dex flew out, containing the legendary Pok\u233?mon data he had compiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Beep~ Kyurem, Dragon/Ice-type, Boundary Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Pressure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Sheer Cold, Glaciate, Outrage, Blizzard, Hyper Voice, Ice Beam, Dragon Pulse, Freeze-Dry, Scale Shot...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: A hero waiting to fill its lost body with truth and ideals, the legendary Ice Dragon Pok\u233?mon.'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So strong!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie listened to the Rotom Pok\u233?dex's introduction and gripped Dylan's clothes tighter. This was the legendary Ice Dragon, Kyurem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The strongest dragon on land."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan held Lillie's small hand to reassure her, then walked towards Kyurem with her slowly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Buzzing~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It seemed that the geometric snowflakes swirling in the sky noticed the two uninvited guests, emitting a low hum before calming down again, as if afraid of disturbing something.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it was already too late.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan could feel Lillie's hand suddenly tightening around his. That was because the massive gray dragon ahead had opened its eyes at some point, its golden, majestic gaze fixed on the two of them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kyurem had awakened!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The entire glacial valley seemed to fall silent at this moment!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under the overwhelming, oppressive atmosphere, even the air seemed to grow thick. Lillie felt like she had to use all her strength just to breathe\u8212?the pressure was immense!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roar~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A ferocious roar echoed across the sky, deafeningly loud. The sound waves generated by the roar surged forward, causing the entire glacial valley to tremble slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So terrifying! This was just a roar!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie shielded her face with her hand, the biting wind stinging her cheeks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The gray dragon slowly rose, towering over the two humans who dared to approach it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kyurem's golden dragon eyes glowed with a frightening light as it stared directly at Dylan. It could feel it! It could sense it clearly!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"White Dragon! You dare to appear before me!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The hoarse, deep voice resonated telepathically throughout the valley. It was Kyurem's voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had sensed the presence of the white dragon emanating from this human.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Has my kindness for the past two thousand years made you too bold?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kyurem lowered its head slightly, its face twisted into a terrifying snarl, enough to make a child cry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It hadn't gone out of its way to find and devour the black and white dragons, which was its act of mercy toward them. And now, the white dragon dared to come before it on its own. Was this a provocation?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't be angry, Kyurem. We don't intend to disturb your slumber."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan smiled as he spoke, releasing a gentle aura, but Kyurem's demeanor remained hostile, though at least it hadn't attacked outright.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was already a good outcome\u8212?after all, this was the legendary Ice Dragon, Kyurem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I am Dylan, Reshiram's partner. We came here specifically for you, Kyurem."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hah~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kyurem sneered. It could already guess that Zekrom and Reshiram would normally avoid it at all costs, so why would they suddenly seek it out?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Kyurem, the strongest dragon of Unova's legends, sleeping in a place like this for so long\u8230? Don't you think that's a waste?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan glanced around at the surroundings. The pristine, immaculate glacial valley was a magnificent sight, but this had been Kyurem's home for thousands of years.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Your power is so overwhelming, incredibly alluring. Even Reshiram and Zekrom have left behind legends passed down through the generations."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As the strongest dragon, isn't it a shame that no one acknowledges you, Kyurem?" Dylan spoke slowly to Kyurem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In response, Kyurem merely scoffed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What a ridiculous statement."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kyurem's golden dragon eyes stared at the human chosen by the White Dragon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why would I need validation from weak ants like humans? Only the worthless care about such things."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The White Dragon and the Black Dragon are both fools. What truth? What ideals?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kyurem slowly straightened up, and its hoarse, resentful telepathic voice grew more dangerous.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It held nothing but contempt for the Black and White Dragons, who were constantly at odds over laughable concepts like truth and ideals. It was almost enough to make a dragon laugh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Weak White Dragon, weak Black Dragon, and their feeble principles and existence."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Relying on frail humans to affirm their value\u8212?what right do those worthless beings have to be compared with me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Frost began to emanate from Kyurem's body, and its presence grew heavier.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pathetic creatures. Then again, I have let them be for over two thousand years. Perhaps it is time to bring them back."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the end, as far as Kyurem was concerned, the so-called White and Black Dragons were no better than this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Reshiram, it seems Kyurem holds you in low regard."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
