If Kyurem really did try to absorb Reshiram, Dylan would immediately have Necrozma intervene.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If you could hold out a little longer and deal some real damage, with Necrozma's help, we'd have a much better chance of catching Kyurem today."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan had a clear reason for sending White Dragon into battle first. He wanted to see how powerful it was and hoped that if White Dragon could hold its own against Kyurem for a while, it could gather useful information about Kyurem's strengths and weaknesses.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, Dylan didn't expect that without the DNA Splicers, Reshiram couldn't even last a few moves against Kyurem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was clear that the gap between even legendary Pok\u233?mon like Reshiram and top-tier legendaries like Kyurem was far greater than Dylan had imagined.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's okay, Dylan. Even though I can't beat Kyurem, next time we face Zekrom, leave it to me!" Reshiram said, awkwardly turning its head. Although its condition wasn't bad, it could still hold out for a bit longer in the fight if necessary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it really didn't want to battle Kyurem\u8212?there was no point in seeking a beating!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's eyelid twitched. He decided to lower his expectations for his ride and backup. He would have to rely on the real main force.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, the aftermath of Photon Geyser and Blizzard was still surging violently.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So powerful!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even from a safe distance, the powerful wind blew toward Dylan and Lillie, leaving Lillie speechless in awe.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What they saw was a strange scene where golden and icy blue energy tides clashed, shattering the cliffs below due to the impact of the energy waves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Terrifying!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roar!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, White Kyurem wasn't satisfied with the situation. Its violent roar echoed as it charged into the sky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a flash, a streak of blue lightning passed over its body, and in the blink of an eye, a black-gray dragon Pok\u233?mon appeared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its massive, muscular body had arms and wings that were part ice and part black. It was none other than Black Kyurem!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Beep~ Black Kyurem, Dragon/Ice-type, Boundary Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Teravolt\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Signature Moves: Freeze Shock, Outrage, Blizzard, Fusion Bolt, Dragon Claw, Scale Shot, Avalanche, Shadow Claw...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: It is said to fight for the ideal world that Pok\u233?mon and humans will achieve in the future. (Black Kyurem)'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's Rotom Dex dutifully explained Black Kyurem's information.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Kyurem has this form too?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie was shocked. This meant that Kyurem had three forms, including its normal state!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A Kyurem that can transform at will is truly amazing," Dylan couldn't help but marvel. This was why it was called the strongest dragon on Earth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Normally, in each generation of Pok\u233?mon, the third legendary could easily overwhelm the other two.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For example, Rayquaza could defeat both the land and sea titans without much effort. Giratina could suppress Dialga and Palkia, and Kyurem could effortlessly crush Reshiram and Zekrom. Even Zygarde's Pok\u233?dex entry mentioned its power surpassing Xerneas and Yveltal, and its ability Aura Break signified its advantage over the two.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Necrozma could also easily overpower the sun and moon gods, and Eternatus\u8212?well, Eternatus was an exception.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Sword and Shield kings were particularly strong against Eternatus, especially Zacian, whose strength was specifically geared towards Eternatus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steel-types are immune to Poison, Fairy-types are immune to Dragon, and coupled with the equally strong Zamazenta, what could Eternatus do?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then there's the ninth generation's Terapagos, with Koraidon and Miraidon clearly not on par with it. Although Terapagos didn't perform outstandingly, it was still the "source of Terastallization."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It's hard to judge the strength of third legendaries across regions, but a Kyurem that can transform freely is definitely not weak. If Kyurem could absorb both Zekrom and Reshiram to return to its true dragon form, it would at least be on par with Ultra Necrozma.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But for now, it wasn't there yet, and besides, Necrozma wasn't in its ultimate form either.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"We still have to fight. Even though there's a level gap, Kyurem isn't in its perfect form yet, having not fully absorbed Zekrom and Reshiram," Dylan thought, narrowing his eyes. This ice dragon's greatest strength was its ability to freely switch between its Black and White forms. Black Kyurem excelled at close combat, while White Kyurem specialized in ranged attacks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Kyurem wasn't in its fused form with Zekrom and Reshiram, so Dawn Wings Necrozma might still stand a chance\u8212?since it was fully fused with Lunala.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A legal 2v1!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
