161: Chapter 161: this time was just an accident\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes, I'll wait for an opportunity to spar with Dylan and collect his Gym Badge as a keepsake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder thought about this, though it seemed a bit odd for a regional champion to challenge a Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But apparently, over in Galar, their Gym Leaders often compete alongside their undefeated champion Leon, so it's not that strange after all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, back in the battle arena\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey calmed herself and finally sent out her trump card, the last of her four Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Excadrill!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a flash of white light, a dark brown Pok\u233?mon landed in front of Lacey. It had a robust body, a white face, and its most striking feature\u8212?sharp steel blades on its forehead and claws. This was Excadrill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is this one a Fairy-type too?" Lillie asked, puzzled as she observed the fierce-looking Excadrill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It didn't look like one at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
'Beep~ Excadrill, Ground/Steel type, Subterranean Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Mold Breaker\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Horn Drill, Drill Run, Swords Dance, Dig, Rock Slide, Slash, Terastallization Burst, Rapid Spin, High Horsepower\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: Its drill-like steel body can penetrate iron plates, making it a vital part of tunnel engineering.'\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No Fairy-type, huh? Well, that makes sense. Bringing an Excadrill into a Fairy-type team isn't all that unusual.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie blinked and remembered her brother's strategies, and it no longer seemed so strange.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gym Leader Dylan, our Blueberry Academy is the sister school to Orange Academy, so our students are also proficient in Terastallization."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey took out a black Tera Orb and addressed Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm aware."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan smiled and nodded. Terastallization was a power developed by Professor Sada and Professor Turo from the Paldea region. Essentially, it allows a Pok\u233?mon's type to change to its Tera Type. Every Pok\u233?mon has a specific Tera Type, and Terastallization transforms it into that type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For example, Lacey's Excadrill was naturally Ground and Steel, but its Tera Type was Fairy. Once Terastallized, it would become a Fairy-type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After Terastallization, its strengths and weaknesses would change to match the Fairy-type, but it could still get STAB (Same-Type Attack Bonus) for using Ground- and Steel-type moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the Tera Type matches the Pok\u233?mon's natural type, the power boost would be even greater. For instance, if this Excadrill Terastallized into its Ground or Steel type, it would gain extra power\u8212?effectively boosting its battle strength.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In comparison to Mega Evolution, Z-Moves, and Dynamaxing, Terastallization offered more tactical flexibility, which was one of its major advantages.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While Terastallization doesn't inherently increase a Pok\u233?mon's raw strength, it's a powerful tool. Take Gyarados, for example. It's undoubtedly strong among Water-types, but its fatal weakness to Electric moves drags it down significantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, if Gyarados Terastallized into a pure Water-type, it would not only enhance its Water-type moves but also reduce its Electric-type weakness from 4x to 2x, making it much more formidable than one might expect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's the advantage of Terastallization.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You truly are knowledgeable, Gym Leader Dylan," Lacey said as the black Tera Orb in her hand began to glow. She had initially thought she might need to explain Terastallization, unsure if Dylan was familiar with it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it turned out there was no need.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Excadrill!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey tossed the Tera Orb towards her Excadrill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The moment the orb touched Excadrill, radiant energy enveloped its entire body, forming crystal-like structures.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What is that?" Lillie asked, stunned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's Terastallization from Paldea. It changes a Pok\u233?mon's type," Alder explained, intrigued as he watched the transformation process.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder had some knowledge of it. It was, after all, a way to enhance a Pok\u233?mon's abilities, similar to Galar's Dynamaxing or Alola's Z-Moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, unlike Dynamaxing, which could only be used in energy spots in Galar, Terastallization had no such limitations. Alder had even pulled some strings to get a Tera Orb for himself, and he found it quite interesting, especially with the tactical flexibility it offered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Crrrrack!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sound of shattering crystals echoed as Terastallized Excadrill emerged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its entire body gleamed with a crystalline glow, but the most eye-catching feature was the pink, heart-shaped crown atop its head\u8212?a hallmark of the Fairy Tera Type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A Fairy Terastallized Excadrill, so it's a pure Fairy-type team?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After Alder's explanation, Lillie understood, though she found it rather peculiar\u8212?but not entirely wrong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Excadrill, Dig!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey quickly commanded her Excadrill after thinking for a moment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Excadrill dived into the ground with incredible speed, disappearing beneath the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Take to the air," Dylan said with a light chuckle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dig allows Ground-type Pok\u233?mon to burrow underground, but a well-timed Earthquake would make Excadrill regret that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unfortunately, Darkrai doesn't know Earthquake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Darkrai floated into the air, its blue eyes calmly watching the ground below, waiting for Excadrill to resurface.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Excadrill, Terastallization Burst!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey gave another order when she saw Darkrai wasn't giving Excadrill any openings.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The ground beneath Darkrai bulged as Excadrill emerged, its body glowing with pink Fairy-type energy. With a heavy swipe of its claws, a beam of light from Terastallization Burst shot towards Darkrai.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fairy-type Terastallization Burst!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Terastallization Burst is normally a Normal-type move, but once a Pok\u233?mon Terastallizes, the move's type changes to match the Pok\u233?mon's Tera Type. It also adapts based on whether the user's Attack or Special Attack is higher.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In Excadrill's case, its Terastallization Burst was, naturally, Attack-based.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thunder."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
