"So please, Miss Lacey, choose one. I recognize your talent and will as a trainer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan took out five beautiful, delicate little brocade boxes from his spatial bag and gestured for Lacey to pick one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These were the five new badges currently available at the Rota Gym: Poison, Dark, Ghost, Dragon, and Legend.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But I..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey snapped back to reality, feeling flustered as she looked at the five little brocade boxes in front of her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She was really embarrassed!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the daughter of Clay, she knew that a Gym Leader didn't necessarily have to be defeated for a badge to be awarded\u8212?if the Gym Leader recognized the challenger, they could still give their badge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But in this Gym Challenge, she had lost so miserably...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could someone like her really deserve the Rota Badge? Lacey's face flushed with embarrassment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hahaha~ Lacey, just pick one. You took a beating from legendary Pok\u233?mon\u8212?getting a badge to make up for it is fair enough."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder laughed, teasing her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And since Dylan recognizes you, there's no need to doubt yourself. Against that team, even if it were me, the result wouldn't have been much different."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder crossed his arms and seriously commented. And he wasn't wrong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Forget about the absurd dragons, Reshiram and Kyurem\u8212?just that Darkrai alone was already Champion-level.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder sincerely believed that if he were up against that Darkrai, even his ace Volcarona would struggle in a hard-fought battle, and he wasn't even sure he could win.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just accept it, Lacey. After becoming stronger, you can challenge Dylan again to show him your growth\u8212?that would be the best way to repay his trust in you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clay also encouraged his precious daughter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I understand! I will not let down Gym Leader Dylan's trust!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Gym Leader's willingness to give his badge to a challenger was a deep form of trust, and for the first time, Lacey felt the joy of being recognized by a powerful trainer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it also meant that she had to work even harder, not to let this recognition go to waste, and to make sure others didn't think Dylan had poor judgment!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm looking forward to it. Now, go ahead and pick one\u8212?or leave it to chance. One of these boxes contains the most precious Rota Legend Badge."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan nodded in satisfaction and then spoke gently.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There's actually a Legend Rota Badge!!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey's beautiful eyes immediately lit up, and Alder and Clay were equally astonished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Legend Rota Badge was undoubtedly the most special. The other Rota Badges could be obtained through normal challenges, but this Legend Badge\u8230? who in the world could defeat Dylan and his team of legendary Pok\u233?mon?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The only way was to get the golden Legend team and earn Dylan's recognition, and then to draw it randomly from these Rota badges.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its rarity was unimaginable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey's breathing quickened. If she could draw this Legend Badge, she would likely be the only person in the world to have it!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A one-in-five chance! Could she do it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, Lacey, trust me, pick this one! It's definitely the right one!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder was excited, pointing to the box in the middle. The thrill of this blind draw was just too much.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"After all, I was the one who picked the golden Legend team for you earlier, wasn't I, Lacey? Believe me!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey couldn't help but glare at Alder when she heard that. You still have the nerve to mention it! Thank you very much!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Alder wasn't wrong\u8212?he had indeed chosen the golden Legend team for her earlier, so...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey bit her lip, her gloved hand trembling slightly as she reached for the middle box.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan handed her the box and put away the other four.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lacey took a deep breath, slowly opening it as Alder and Clay curiously leaned in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The box opened, revealing a beautifully crafted green gemstone badge with a deep purple Poison-type emblem on top.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a Poison Rota Badge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh? It's Poison?" Alder scratched his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No way, his instincts were usually spot-on. What a pity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But suddenly, Alder felt a sharp, blade-like gaze directed at him. Yep, it was from the adorable Lacey.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Uh... Lacey, this time was just an accident," Alder said awkwardly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Champion Alder," Lacey said with a blank expression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you so much for your help today!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ahhh! I was so close to the Legend Rota Badge!! Ahhhh!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
