Description: Though its body has shrunk, its power has grown immeasurable. With just a slight use of its psychic abilities, even skyscrapers could be reduced to ashes. (Shiny Mega Mewtwo Y)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Rotom Pok\u233?dex displayed Shiny Mewtwo Y's information, and Dylan nodded in satisfaction. Not bad at all!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This Mega Stone is yours now, Mewtwo," Dylan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A flash of light enveloped Shiny Mewtwo Y as it reverted to its normal form. Without hesitation, it absorbed the Mega Stone into its body, ensuring that it could Mega Evolve whenever it wished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since today was Sunday, the Rota Gym was closed, meaning Dylan didn't have to open for business.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Initially, Dylan planned to take Lillie out for breakfast, but as soon as they stepped out of the gym's entrance\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh? Brother, look over there," Lillie pointed toward the corner near the gym, her voice filled with curiosity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan followed her gaze and raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What are you doing here?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He and Lillie walked over, looking curiously at the red-haired boy standing in the corner, lost in thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's none of your business," the boy replied coldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was a sharp-featured youth with pale skin and messy red hair. His aura was overwhelmingly cold and distant, making it clear he wasn't the type to welcome company.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This guy seems really unfriendly\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie frowned slightly. He was standing right outside their home\u8212?how could it have nothing to do with them?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At this point, Lillie had already subconsciously started seeing the Rota Gym as her home.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh? You're not here to see me? Silver?" Dylan asked, intrigued as he examined the red-haired boy\u8212?Silver.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Silver's expression changed instantly. He instinctively stepped back, his body tensing like a wary beast sensing danger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But he quickly regained his composure, his gaze turning doubtful as he looked at Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You are\u8230? Dylan?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Silver wasn't foolish\u8212?he was actually quite sharp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Leaf sent you to find me, and yet you don't even know what I look like?" Dylan sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And why are you so late? Leaf told me you should've arrived within two or three days."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Silver pressed his lips together and remained silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Grrr~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, an awkward grumble echoed from Silver's stomach. His head dropped lower, his ears turning red as he felt Dylan and Lillie's amused gazes on him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I\u8230? lost my phone and wallet on the way here\u8230?" he muttered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Seriously?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan sighed and rubbed his forehead. Oh well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come with me. Since you're Leaf's little brother, that makes you my little brother too. Let's grab some food first, then you can get some rest\u8212?you probably haven't had a proper sleep in a while, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He patted Silver's frost-covered clothes, realizing the boy must have been standing outside for quite some time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Silver instinctively flinched at the touch, reluctant to let others get too close\u8212?likely a habit from his rough upbringing. But he remembered what his sister, Leaf, had said: Dylan is someone you can trust completely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And besides, he could sense genuine kindness from Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I woke up early this morning," Silver muttered stubbornly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If you got here so early, why didn't you knock on the door?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?" Silver remained silent. He wasn't good at this kind of thing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan took Silver and Lillie to a nearby breakfast shop and ordered Silver a large bowl of noodles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eat slowly. If you're still hungry, I'll get you another bowl. Afterward, we'll go buy you some new clothes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan smiled warmly at Silver, while Lillie curiously observed her new acquaintance\u8212?Leaf's younger brother.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?Thanks," Silver said hesitantly. He stopped eating for a moment, seemingly struggling to get the words out, before finally murmuring his gratitude.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No need to be polite. From now on, you'll be my apprentice\u8212?Leaf told you about that, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Silver nodded. He was still skeptical about whether Dylan could truly stand against the Masked Man, but he trusted Leaf. And so far, he was starting to trust Dylan as well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After breakfast, Dylan took Silver shopping for clothes before returning to the Rota Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Silver stepped out after changing into his new outfit and tidying up his hair, he looked like a completely different person.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dressed in a fitted deep-purple high-necked long-sleeve and matching purple pants, his now neatly combed red hair accentuated his sharp, defiant demeanor. The transformation made his cold and rebellious aura even more pronounced.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not bad, looking sharp," Dylan said, eyeing Silver with approval.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?" Silver looked away, rubbing his nose awkwardly. He wasn't used to this kind of praise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But for the first time\u8212?aside from Leaf\u8212?he felt a warmth from someone else.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"From today onward, you're part of the Rota Gym, Silver. Welcome aboard."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan grinned and patted Silver's shoulder.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He planned to train Silver well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And when Silver was ready, Dylan would send him to challenge Giovanni.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oh, I can't wait to see Giovanni's face when that happens.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was going to be interesting\u8212?after all, Silver was Giovanni's ultimate counter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
