For a company, a high-tech research expert like Kukui was invaluable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even though Dylan already had Colress, recruiting Kukui was a huge win.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a hearty meal, Kukui said his goodbyes and left.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You two didn't just come to Alola for a vacation, did you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto lit a cigarette, crossed his legs, and looked leisurely at Dylan and Lillie.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He and Amelia had spent over a month traveling Hoenn, and Lillie never once mentioned wanting to return to Alola.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So they came back by themselves. Compared to Kanto, Alola's natural beauty made it perfect for retirement. They'd even decided to settle down here.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's about Lillie's family," Dylan shrugged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm sorry, godfather, godmother\u8230? I actually ran away from Aether Foundation. I'm sorry I kept it from you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie stood up and bowed deeply in apology.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ran away? Did Lusamine mistreat you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto wasn't surprised she was from the Aether Foundation. He was more concerned about her use of the word "ran away."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"We knew your background a long time ago, Lillie. You just didn't tell us\u8212?so you must've had your reasons."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Amelia gently pulled Lillie down to sit beside her, patting her hand with a kind smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They weren't fools. Of course they investigated Lillie's background after taking her in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turns out, she was the daughter of Lusamine, Aether Foundation's president. A real-life fallen noblewoman.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the reason for her fall from grace remained a mystery\u8212?until now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's mother. She wanted to use Nebby to open an Ultra Wormhole."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie bit her lip, her big, clear eyes reddening slightly. She was clearly emotional\u8212?but far stronger than before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ultra Wormhole?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto stroked his chin thoughtfully. Amelia, however, looked completely lost.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's an Ultra Wormhole?" Leaf also looked confused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's a unique phenomenon in the Alola region. It connects our world to Ultra Space."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan offered an explanation. Knowledge of Ultra Space was very limited in this world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Like a parallel dimension?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The group was stunned. Was this about to become a sci-fi story?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You could say that. You can also think of it as a parallel universe or subdimension. But these days, there aren't many living beings left in Ultra Space."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan nodded. Ultra Space was actually a general term\u8212?it encompassed many different realms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like Nihilego's Ultra Deep Sea, Guzzlord's Ultra Ruin, and Poipole's Ultra Megalopolis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only Ultra Megalopolis and Ultra Ruin were known to have human civilizations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ultra Megalopolis basically destroyed itself. They stole Necrozma's light and sealed the weakened beast in a tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without Necrozma, their world fell into darkness and ruin. Today, the population of Ultra Megalopolis is nearly extinct.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ultra Ruin was even worse\u8212?a polluted wasteland. Toxic air, poisoned water.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its people had to wear hazmat suits and use purification systems to survive. Eventually, they migrated to another planet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzzlord remained in the ruins, where it's known as the Glutton.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So aliens really do exist." Itto was fascinated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They do\u8212?and their technology is far more advanced than ours."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan agreed. It was fair to call the people of Ultra Megalopolis and Ultra Ruin aliens.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their tech was far superior. The Ultra Recon Squad could "ride space" between dimensions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the Ultra Ruin people had already performed interplanetary migration.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So what's the problem with opening an Ultra Wormhole?" Amelia asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There's a big problem. Dad, do you know why Alola never formed a Pok\u233?mon League?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I never looked into it," Itto shrugged. Politics weren't his thing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's because of the Ultra Beasts from Ultra Space."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan got straight to the point.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ultra Beasts are Pok\u233?mon from Ultra Space. They have dangerous instincts and pose a threat to ordinary people."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ten years ago, the Pok\u233?mon League sent the International Police to Alola to investigate Guzzlord\u8212?and someone died on that mission."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"With so many unknowns, the League wasn't about to set up shop here."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan continued, mentioning how Anabel was found unconscious on a beach by Looker and Nanu after the Guzzlord incident.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She'd lost all her memories\u8212?except her name.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes, the same Anabel Dylan had met at the Battle Pyramid\u8212?frontier brain and part-time International Police.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to the games, no one knew if Anabel was originally from this world or from Ultra Space. She fell through an Ultra Wormhole.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She ended up working under Looker. Eventually, she was promoted\u8212?and became his boss.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yup. Looker literally found his future boss washed up on a beach.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I see\u8230? But Dylan, how do you know all this?" Itto was amazed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Read more. Talk more. Ask more questions." Dylan shrugged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto rolled his eyes. What a load of crap. But whatever\u8212?Dylan was smart. He'd figure it out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So you're here to help Lillie confront her mother, Lusamine? That woman's tough, but not impossible. Need help?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Itto didn't think much of the Aether Foundation. Sure, they ruled Alola\u8212?but only locally.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Besides, he was now the head of the Silph Company. That's right.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After Giovanni led Team Rocket to take over Silph's headquarters, many shareholders sold their stock under pressure. Dylan and Giovanni bought most of it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That left Itto\u8212?already the biggest shareholder\u8212?in charge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now, the only other shareholders were the president, Dylan, and Giovanni.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sure, a dragon doesn't trample local snakes. But if Lusamine really abused Lillie, Itto wouldn't mind crushing her a bit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No need. Tomorrow, Lillie and I will pay a visit to Aether Paradise."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan said casually. He'd never seen Aether as a real threat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might be a major player in Alola, but they were still just big fish in a small pond.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even back when Dylan first came to Alola, he could've taken Aether down without breaking a sweat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just like Silph crumbled before Team Rocket, Aether couldn't stand against someone like him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lusamine was strong, sure\u8212?a high-tier trainer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Dylan could take her out with ease.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright then. Just be careful." Itto could hear the confidence in Dylan's voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After some more small talk, Dylan took Lillie and Leaf out to explore Hau'oli City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Leaf's first time in Alola, and she found it fascinating.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The next morning\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After breakfast, the three of them flew to Aether Paradise atop the white dragon Reshiram.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Aether Paradise was the Aether Foundation's HQ\u8212?the fifth island of Alola, an artificial island.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, the Foundation had immense wealth and influence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be fair, Lusamine was undeniably capable. She'd turned Aether from obscurity into a major power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Dylan was also thinking\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If things were like in the games, Lusamine had done some things the League would never approve of.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Especially her "collection room," where she kept live Pok\u233?mon frozen as trophies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If that ever got out\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the League\u8212?especially Lance and N\u8212?found out\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Aether Paradise would be wiped clean.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So if he really found that cold storage room\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could he use it to blackmail Lusamine into working for him?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What's that saying again?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ma'am, you wouldn't want your little secret getting out\u8230? would you?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
