319: Chapter 319: Got Taken by Dylan!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside the Saffron Gym, Sabrina stared at the profile of the new head of the Kanto Elite Four.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
'Giovanni \u8211? Head of the Kanto Elite Four}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Specialty: Ground Type'}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni\u8212?{\b
the boss}\u8212?had become the head of the Elite Four. For Sabrina, this was nothing short of a lightning bolt from a clear sky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her head was spinning. Numb.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
How could this have happened?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina's eyes wavered with psychic ripples. She exhaled softly\u8212?perhaps this was fine. With the boss's strength, he'd do just fine in the League.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then suddenly, she tilted her head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hold on. How had Dylan and the boss suddenly been promoted?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What happened to Lance?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, the Kanto League's official website and forums were already ablaze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"We regret to inform you that Lance, Agatha, Bruno, and Lorelei have formally resigned from their positions. We thank them for their many years of service to the Kanto region."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The new Champion and Elite Four of Kanto have now been appointed. They will inherit the will of their predecessors and protect Kanto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This announcement stunned the entire region.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All four members of the Elite Four gone in one day? This was way too sudden.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Agatha, maybe, was reaching retirement age\u8212?but Lance and the other two were in their prime.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why such a coordinated resignation?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Many people immediately sensed something off. Clearly, there was a story here. But since the League wasn't saying anything, all they could do was speculate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the new Champion and Elite Four page, the comments were exploding:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh good, from menace Gym Leader to menace Champion. And he's listed as a Dragon-type specialist too? Incredible."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Waaah! Our Dylan finally made it! Go Dylan! Asha will always support you!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fully approve of Dylan becoming Champion!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I always said Giovanni should've been on the Elite Four!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Never seen these three before. But this Leaf girl is so cute\u8212?she looks really young. Is she really Elite Four material?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Unfamiliar? Just visit the Rota Gym a few times\u8212?you'll get very familiar\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Most comments were positive, though naturally, there were a few skeptics and even trolls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which was to be expected. Lance and his team had massive prestige in Kanto, with tons of fans. Replacing all four without an explanation was bound to ruffle feathers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the League had no plans to explain. What could they say? That Lance had slaughtered half the council and broken ties with the League?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not a chance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside the League HQ, Goodshow led Dylan and the new Elite Four into their office suite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is your designated lounge and office space. If you're staying at the League HQ, housing has been arranged on the Plateau as well," Goodshow said with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan looked around\u8212?everything was new. Fresh furniture, fresh d\u233?cor. Clearly, this was all redone for them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Goodshow, to his credit, wasn't tone-deaf enough to leave behind the "belongings" of the former Four for their replacements.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hard to believe... The Indigo Conference hasn't even started, and I'm already Elite Four," Blue muttered, glancing around.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His original goal after leaving Pallet Town had been to dominate the Kanto League. Now, while he hadn't quite taken the top, he was pretty damn close.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was a huge step forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait, Chairman\u8212?does this mean Red and I can't participate in the Indigo Conference?" Blue suddenly asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They had signed up for the tournament, which was just days away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course not," Goodshow chuckled. "You're Elite Four now. You can't be going down to compete with the kids."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, the Indigo Conference winner earns the right to challenge the Elite Four. If the Elite Four themselves joined, that would make a mockery of the whole process.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(Like in the anime, Ash became Alola Champion because there simply wasn't an Elite Four at the time\u8212?the league was new, and the tournament was funded and organized by the Aether Foundation. The rules weren't even finalized.)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's fine. I don't want to bully rookies anyway," Blue shrugged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, if not for the formal process, he wouldn't have entered. The whole tournament would've been just him vs. Red in the finals anyway.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To the west of Cinnabar Island lay a wide stretch of open sea\u8212?and on it, a crescent-shaped island not marked on any map.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That day, the forgotten isle welcomed several new visitors.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cerise Island... we finally found it," Agatha said, leaning on her cane as she looked toward the dormant volcano at the center.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a bizarre structure, ringed by seven towering stone pillars.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're sure this is it?" Lorelei asked, pushing up her glasses.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They had searched the sea for over a day to find it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
