"Which one?" Lorelei asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Who knows? Ho-Oh, maybe? Or Lugia? We'll know when we summon it," Agatha replied.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kanto had many legendary birds\u8212?the famed trio of Zapdos, Articuno, and Moltres.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the "legendary large bird Pok\u233?mon" were Ho-Oh and Lugia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which one they could summon, Agatha didn't know.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If Lance captures this one, along with Zekrom, he'll be unstoppable," Lorelei said, smirking. "Then our dream will be within reach."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She had left with Lance because they shared the same ideals.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There were too many Pok\u233?mon suffering, too many humans abusing nature. The League was too soft. The wicked should be purged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance stood with arms folded, his black cape fluttering as he gazed at the mountain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"When we summon it... we strike," he said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To rid the world of evil, they needed power. And a legendary bird would grant that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The world must be made clean again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"At this point, the only one who could stop Lance is Dylan," Agatha said with a sly chuckle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But what if Dylan opposes us?" Bruno asked bluntly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had never wanted to leave. He was fine being Elite Four.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So why the hell was he here now, with these lunatics?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oh right\u8212?because Agatha had pulled some trickery on him. And now, even if he wanted to leave, he couldn't.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He really didn't get it. Lance and Lorelei being zealots was one thing. Why was Agatha out here risking her geriatric spine?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And to top it off, Bruno seriously doubted they'd succeed. Last time they tried something big, they got wrecked by Aizen. This time? Probably Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan used to be their most reliable ally\u8212?now they had made him their enemy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno was Tired\u8482?.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan is like us\u8212?devoted to Pok\u233?mon and justice," Lance said calmly, confidence in his voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"???" Bruno was baffled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Justice? Has Lance seen Dylan's online nickname?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The League won't let us kill freely," Bruno reminded them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not everyone deserves death, but to Lance and Lorelei, anything evil must be eradicated. No shades of gray. Only black and white.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The League can't stop us now," Lorelei said coldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With them gone, the League had no strong cards left. Except Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But Dylan is the Champion now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That got everyone's attention. Lance, Lorelei, and Agatha all turned to him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno felt goosebumps rise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"He's Champion. The new Elite Four are in place too. And Dylan's listed as a Dragon-type specialist."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno's tone was strange as he showed them the website.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan, the multi-type master, had chosen Dragon as his official specialization. What did it mean?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance's title. Taken. By Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance's brow twitched.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan... was this a tribute to me, your senior? Truly... you've finally understood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragons. Are. Supreme!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Heh... Goodshow moves fast," Agatha said with a twinkle in her eye.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They'd only been gone two days, and he already replaced them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her gaze landed on Blue's profile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak's grandson, huh...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tch. Just some kids," Lorelei scoffed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, we'll need the badges to activate the island. Let's get them," Agatha said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She was generally level-headed, but even she had things she couldn't let go of. Otherwise, she wouldn't be out here "starting over" with the crazies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wasn't the real issue that Dylan was Champion now?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These three were still plotting\u8212?did they really think Dylan wouldn't flatten them?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno sighed deeply. Maybe it was time to think about an exit strategy. He didn't want to end up in the same cell block as the Rocket Executives.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd rather not get prison-jumped by Archer and company.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And sure, he could probably reverse it and beat them up instead\u8212?but still.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno had always been loyal to the League, dammit!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
End of Chapter 319}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
