And now? Dylan had gone and done it himself. If she wanted to dominate Kanto, didn't that mean she'd have to challenge her own teacher?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That seemed\u8230? kinda hard. Maybe just let Lance come back instead?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pfft\u8212?" The girls nearby, Asha and the others, couldn't help but stifle their giggles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Didn't you say you were going to challenge other regions' Champions?" Dylan asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah well, the plan was Hoenn's Wallace. He looked easy, but then you forced him to retire too!" Selene huffed in frustration.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't worry, I believe in you. I might step down sometime next year anyway. Whether you can become Kanto Champion will depend on your own ability," Dylan said nonchalantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What 'huh'? Hurry up and get stronger. The current Elite Four are way tougher than the last group. You don't want to end up the bottom rank, do you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that, Leaf pouted and muttered under her breath. She definitely felt called out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pfft~! Gym Leader Bro, you're looking down on me! I'm already Champion-tier now! I'm going to be Champion next year!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Selene's voice was full of pride and energy. As long as Dylan wasn't in her way, she wasn't afraid of anyone. Monsters, ghosts, whatever\u8212?she'd crush them all!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Whoa! Selene's Champion-level now?" Asha gasped with delight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh my god, what a freak of nature!" Leaf clutched her head. This was unreal. Selene had only been gone for like two or three months and was already Champion-tier?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That kind of growth rate wasn't just comparable to Red\u8212?it might've been faster, given how solid her foundation was.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Selene's amazing!" Yellow beamed with admiration for her senior disciple.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..." Silver fell silent. If what the others said was true, then Selene had only just started her journey not long ago...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, if he wanted to challenge for the title of Dylan's strongest disciple, it was going to be a long road.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Do you want a beating? How many times do I have to tell you\u8212?you're a girl! Stop calling yourself 'ya boi'!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan sighed in exasperation, laughing despite himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~" Selene giggled shamelessly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How's that Ultra Beast coming along?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's strong! That Kartana you sent me is totally busted! Its Sacred Sword can cut anything!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Judging by her excitement, Dylan started to wonder what exactly she'd been cutting...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yep, he'd sent her a Kartana\u8212?her own choice, actually.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good. When are you coming back to Rota?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Uhh... not for a while. I'm in the Mt. Silver area right now, hoping to find a Tyranitar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright. When you're back, come by the gym. I want to see how much you've grown. Hanging up now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roger that! Bye-bye Gym Leader Bro~ love ya, mwah~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This damn girl. Who did she even learn this nonsense from?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan stared at the call log, feeling vaguely disturbed. His first carefully-raised disciple turned out like this?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At least Asha and Silver were respectful and hardworking. Thank goodness for small blessings.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A week passed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Indigo Conference continued in full swing across all regions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan didn't go watch in person\u8212?instead, he monitored the battles via live stream in the gym's screening room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On screen, Jeanette was currently battling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Watching her Nidoqueen lay down Toxic Spikes and secure victory, Dylan nodded in approval. Jeanette was getting stronger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, I'll give you credit\u8212?you've definitely influenced the meta. These days, 9 out of every 10 Indigo matches feature Poison-types," Leaf commented, eyeing him sideways.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Kanto had more Dark and Ghost-types, she had no doubt those would be booming too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nowadays, even Trainers who weren't Poison-type specialists had to keep one or two Poison or Steel-types in their team.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No one wanted to get caught off guard by a random Beedrill or Golbat spreading Toxic Spikes, or survive a surprise Venoshock only to slowly die of poison stalling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The battle culture in Kanto had been utterly "poisoned" by Dylan's influence. You either adapted or got wrecked. People were building counters specifically for him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm proud," Dylan said with a serene smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Elevating the average quality of Kanto Trainers? That was the ultimate honor for a Gym Leader.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Did you hear? Koga and Surge have been reinstated," Leaf said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah, Lily pulled them back into the group chat," Dylan replied with a nod.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Goodshow really has guts. Those two were Rocket Executives," Leaf marveled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There aren't many replacements for Gym Leaders. And Koga and Surge... are trustworthy," Dylan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He hadn't expected Goodshow to be that bold, though\u8212?bringing them back so quickly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two days ago, Koga and Surge were added back to the Gym Leader chat, and Lily roasted them hard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They got dragged so badly they probably couldn't lift their heads for a day.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But that's gonna bring problems," Dylan said with a dry chuckle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh? What do you mean?" Leaf blinked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If Lance finds out, he won't let it go. Even if they've turned over a new leaf."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Lance's zero-tolerance for evil, there was no way he'd accept former Rocket operatives returning to the League.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The League believed in redemption and second chances.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance did not. To him, Koga and Surge were nothing but filth\u8212?former scum who could never be clean.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turncoats? He'd "cleanse" them personally.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"...Yeah, you're probably right," Leaf muttered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This could blow up," Dylan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the Pok\u233?mon Adventures manga, Lance once used just a Dragonair to annihilate all of Vermilion City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The casualty count was unknown.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In that story, the Kanto Elite Four sought to eliminate humanity to create a perfect world. City-level destruction wasn't out of place.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If things escalated here, Dylan wouldn't be surprised if Lance targeted Vermilion City directly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gym Leader Bro, you've got a challenger. And, um..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Asha's voice came through the intercom.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After hearing the rest, Dylan's expression turned... complicated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Standing before the Rota Gym's roulette wheel was a massive, shirtless man with wild blue hair and sculpted muscles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wore white martial arts pants and black wristbands. His face was rugged. His eyes, serious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Bruno?" Dylan said as he walked out, blinking in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The former third-ranked Elite Four member had arrived.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan... no, Champion Dylan," Bruno corrected himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't call me 'Elite Four' anymore. I'm not one of them."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though Bruno looked like a meathead, he had more brains than people gave him credit for.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd always stayed quiet in the League\u8212?mostly because the other three were complete lunatics.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Plus, Agatha had him under psychic control.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Didn't expect you to come here," Dylan admitted. He and Bruno had only met a few times.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Among the former Elite Four, he was closest with Lance, then Lorelei. Agatha was... complicated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno? They barely spoke.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I had no choice. Lance and the others have completely lost it," Bruno groaned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You have no idea the crap they're planning. I think they've all lost their damn minds."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Champion Dylan, I came to tell you: I'm not like them. I'm normal, okay?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under Dylan's slightly baffled gaze, the muscleman began pouring out his heart.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He hadn't slept well in days.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I believe you, Mr. Bruno," Dylan said with a knowing smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So he'd come to defect, huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looks like Bruno was smarter than he looked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I joined the League to fight strong Trainers and grow alongside my Pok\u233?mon," Bruno sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And instead I get these lunatics rambling about 'vermin' and 'corruption' every day\u8212?it's like they're cursed!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Worst part? That old lady uses hypnosis on me sometimes! What did I do to deserve this?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruno was heartbroken. He'd had such promise\u8212?now it felt like he was headed straight for prison.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which was so not the path he had envisioned for himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm telling you, Champion Dylan\u8212?I'm one of the good guys! A model citizen! Not one of those fanatics!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
End of Chapter 320\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
