342: Chapter 342: The Mythical Darkest Day!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The battle between Dylan and Leon was over, and word of the match\u8212?and its outcome\u8212?spread like wildfire across the world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
News articles and forum threads began popping up like mushrooms after rain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All across the regions, online forums were abuzz. Countless trainers flooded Galar's forums just to enjoy the show.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"LMAO\u8212?y'all hyped up the 'Unbeaten Champion' 24/7, but the guy couldn't even take a single win off Kanto's Champion Dylan. What a joke."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You laughing at what, exactly? Fine, Kanto fans can gloat, but you? A Kalos trainer? Why don't you send Diantha over here and let's see if Leon doesn't wipe the floor with her!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oof, someone's mad. What gives you the right to compare your boy Leon to Diantha? Just 'cause he got steamrolled by Dylan?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Psh, anyone with a brain could see Dylan's just too strong."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly! Kanto supremacy, baby!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The forums were in flames.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Many Galar fans were understandably disgruntled\u8212?the loss was humiliating.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But there were still plenty of Galar loyalists who stood their ground. Leon was beloved in Galar. He had the respect of nearly every trainer there.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So sure, he lost to Dylan. Fine. Dylan was Kanto's Champion, and Kanto had always been the seat of the Pok\u233?mon League. Losing to someone like him wasn't shameful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the sheer one-sidedness of the battle? Yeah, that stung.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, what right did other regions have to laugh? You think your Champions wouldn't get steamrolled just the same?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Please.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yeah\u8230? the internet in Galar had exploded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, Dylan was completely unaware of the online chaos. After the match, he returned backstage to rest. Once Lillie and Leaf arrived, the three joined Leon and headed for Rose Tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Chairman Rose was already waiting in his executive office.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Truly impressive, Dylan. Absolutely incredible."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He applauded warmly. He'd always known Dylan was strong, but having witnessed his battle with Leon\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He now understood: this guy wasn't just strong. He was inhuman.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oleana served tea, her usually indifferent eyes resting on Dylan with\u8230? a distinctly wary glint.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In her view? Dylan was a monster. Even Leon looked like a green rookie next to him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You flatter me, Chairman," Dylan replied humbly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, no flattery here. I'm sure Leon agrees," Rose said in his deep, composed voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon gave a helpless smile but nodded in agreement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Still\u8230? I'm afraid our public image in Galar might take a bit of a hit."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rose knew the optics were going to be rough. Leon hadn't just lost\u8212?he'd been demolished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that wasn't Leon's fault. It was Dylan's\u8212?for being on an entirely different level.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Leon is plenty strong," Dylan said. "Turning that narrative around is easy. Just have him battle another Champion from a different region and win clean. That'll shut down all the noise."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a simple fix.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon was powerful. All he needed was a solid win to remind the world of that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You really think Leon is that strong?" Rose looked intrigued.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon groaned, pinching the bridge of his nose. Why did that sound so weird coming from his boss?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course he knew Rose wasn't mocking him. But it did feel ironic\u8212?after being utterly flattened, someone was calling him strong?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course. Out of all the trainers I know, only Lance and Giovanni could rival him."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan said it plainly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rose's eyes twinkled with amusement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You can just call me Leon," Leon interjected. "And\u8230? Giovanni? You mean the Viridian Gym Leader? He's the current head of Kanto's Elite Four, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Correct," Dylan replied with a nod. "If you ever visit Kanto, I can introduce you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Deal!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon agreed without hesitation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Compared to Dylan, he was far more curious about Lance and Giovanni. Once was enough when it came to battling Dylan and those terrifying dragons.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unless\u8230? Dylan didn't bring out those legendaries next time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, what are your plans next?" Rose asked, smiling. "Shall I give you a tour of Galar?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh?" Dylan raised a brow. "Where to?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Stow-on-Side."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's gaze flickered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Stow-on-Side\u8212?once the heart of Galar\u8212?was rich in ancient history and home to Galar's strongest Gym: Raihan's.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that wasn't the important part.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What mattered was what lay beneath it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then I'd be honored," Dylan agreed with a smile. He was curious what Rose wanted to show him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, right. Leon, this is for you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As if remembering something, Dylan pulled out a small velvet box and handed it over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A badge?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon opened it and blinked in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside was a deep blue emblem in the shape of a stylized dragon's head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Dragon\u8212?Rota Badge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're giving me a badge?" Leon asked, baffled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A very expensive one at that," Rose chuckled. "I've heard the Rota Badges are worth over ten million Pok\u233?."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, that meant nothing to Rose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What made them valuable was that you could only earn one by battling Dylan and gaining his approval.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just a memento. If you want the other badges later, come challenge me again," Dylan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon fell into thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So to earn the other elemental Rota Badges, he'd just need to challenge Dylan's non-dragon lineups.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meaning\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wouldn't have to fight those dragons again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His eyes lit up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Perfect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Great! I'll challenge you in Kanto someday!" Leon said, stowing the badge with renewed vigor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If he didn't have to face the legendaries again, he'd gladly battle Dylan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll be waiting," Dylan replied with a grin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After chatting a while longer, Rose treated them to a hearty lunch. Dylan, Lillie, and Leaf then returned to their villa.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan checked his phone: tons of missed calls and congratulatory messages. He replied to each one before hopping into the shower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, Leaf and Lillie were sprawled on the couch, gleefully scrolling through all the chaos on the forums.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Calyrex was also staring at a phone nearby\u8212?completely absorbed in its chess game.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The next morning, Rose arranged two Flying Taxis and headed for Stow-on-Side.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They arrived around noon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Stow-on-Side was a fascinating city, a blend of medieval ruins and vibrant local culture. The architecture had a strong historical flair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As they walked through the streets, Rose narrated the city's long history with his usual eloquent charm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Soon, his tone shifted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan," he said, "I heard you're quite well-read on regional history. Is that true?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not especially," Dylan replied modestly. "I just loved books growing up, so I've picked up a bit here and there."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then you've surely heard of the disaster that struck Galar 3,000 years ago?" Rose asked smoothly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaf and Lillie perked up at that, curious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course," Dylan nodded. "Three thousand years ago, a Pok\u233?mon tried to absorb Galar's energy to survive. It brought about the phenomenon known as the Darkest Day."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A black vortex appeared in the sky, enveloping the region and triggering widespread destruction."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rose looked surprised. Dylan really did know.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The vortex caused many Pok\u233?mon to undergo uncontrolled, extreme Gigantamax transformations. They went berserk, ravaging everything."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Galar fell into chaos. It almost led to the region's collapse."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That means\u8230? the Pok\u233?mon that caused it was the origin of Gigantamax energy?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie immediately connected the dots.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just like how Terapagos was the source of Tera Energy in Paldea, this Pok\u233?mon must've been behind Dynamax.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly," Rose said, impressed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So what happened after that?" Leaf asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"At the height of the crisis," Rose explained, "two heroes appeared\u8212?wielding a sword and shield\u8212?and together they defeated the beast, saving the region."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was the Galarian legend.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The heroes of old had vanquished the dark Pok\u233?mon and restored peace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Are you interested in that Pok\u233?mon, Dylan?" Rose asked meaningfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan raised an eyebrow. "Chairman Rose, do you know where it is?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come with me," Rose said with a knowing smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This time, he didn't take them sightseeing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Instead, they headed to Stow-on-Side Stadium.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From there, Rose led them to a hidden underground facility via elevator.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is the Power Plant," he explained. "It supplies Dynamax energy to every stadium across Galar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The energy here is vital. Access is strictly limited."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He guided them through the corridors\u8212?until they reached a steel door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But the most important thing in this facility\u8230?" Rose typed in a passcode. The door slowly creaked open, revealing a crimson glow from within.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?isn't the energy itself."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's this: the legendary Pok\u233?mon that nearly destroyed Galar 3,000 years ago\u8212?Eternatus!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A massive, nightmarish skeletal dragon lay coiled within the chamber, its form pulsing with ominous red light.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The bringer of the Darkest Day.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The origin of Dynamax.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Eternatus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's eyes lit up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Poison/Dragon-type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
