348: Chapter 348: Time to Go Back\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be honest, Dylan was feeling quite conflicted. Personally, he preferred the Single Strike Style a bit more, but that glaring four-times weakness to Fairy-type attacks was a serious flaw.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The reason Mustard's Gigantamax Urshifu lost to Dynamax Iron Valiant earlier was precisely because of that fatal vulnerability.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Rapid Strike Style was definitely more practical overall, mainly because it didn't have such a pronounced weakness.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's let Kubfu choose for himself when the time comes. Which path he evolves down should be up to him."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan rubbed Kubfu's head with a smile\u8212?he had to admit, the little guy had a great feel to him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Baah!" Kubfu's eyes lit up at that, sparkling with excitement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This Trainer is so kind! He actually respects me!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hahaha~ Well said. Whether it's Rapid Strike or Single Strike, both are incredibly strong in their own right."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mustard blinked for a moment, then chuckled in satisfaction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He suddenly felt that handing Kubfu over to Dylan had been an incredibly wise decision. Absolutely the right call!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With the important matters settled, Honey went to prepare dinner, and Mustard naturally insisted on having Dylan and the others stay for the meal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tch\u8212?got matched with that cheater again." Suddenly, Mustard started muttering in annoyance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cheater?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was holding his phone. Dylan glanced over\u8212?it looked like he was playing a Go app.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mustard, as it turned out, was actually quite fond of video games. His profile even mentioned it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I've been matched against this guy multiple times. He's definitely cheating. Who even cheats in Go of all games?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He grumbled as he exited the app, clearly frustrated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And his username, too. 'The Lone King'\u8212?kids these days are seriously over the top."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mustard shook his head in disapproval at the 'edgelord' tendencies of Galar's modern youth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's wrong with you guys?" Mustard frowned at the weird looks from Dylan and the others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan looked\u8230? conflicted. Lillie and Leaf, having heard what Mustard said, had also gone stiff with awkward expressions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, seated beside Dylan, Calyrex casually glanced at Mustard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
I am a king by nature. Even if I no longer rule Galar, I am still Calyrex. What part of that is "edgelord"?!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
And I wasn't cheating! I wasn't!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, Calyrex wasn't going to argue over something so petty. His pride wasn't that fragile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Master Mustard, the World Championship will be held next year. Are you planning to participate?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan deftly shifted the topic. After all, Calyrex was right there.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was already the end of the year\u8212?Mustard had surely heard about the tournament. After all, Leon was his student.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was Galar's big opportunity to make a splash on the world stage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be fair, Galar had plenty of Champion-tier trainers. Leon was especially strong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon, Raihan, Mustard, Peony\u8212?four Champion-level trainers, not even counting Gloria.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If it weren't for the monster-level trainers in Kanto, Galar could very well be the strongest region.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But in reality, both Mustard and Peony had very low public visibility now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mustard had retired long ago, his dojo secluded. Most people outside a niche group didn't even know his name anymore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Peony was even more obscure. Though he had once served as Galar Champion, he resigned shortly after Rose became Chairman, due to their personal conflict.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Peony's rise had been meteoric, but so was his retirement. It had been many years since then, and few even remembered him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Aside from those four canon Champion-tier trainers, Gloria and Hop were both prodigies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gloria aside, Hop\u8212?Leon's younger brother\u8212?was basically born with a cheat code. Though in the early and mid-game of {\i
Sword and Shield}, he constantly lost to Gloria and was even crushed by Bede to the point of losing confidence...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
By the end, he rose rapidly, rekindling his fighting spirit. He even tamed the legendary Zamazenta, becoming one of the rare few acknowledged by a legendary Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"World Championship, huh? Sigh\u8230? This old man's bones are getting up there, you know."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mustard rested his chin in his hand. He had been thinking about it. He was tempted\u8212?but it also felt a bit out of place for an old-timer to be competing against youth for ranking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But your heart isn't old, Master." Dylan smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hahaha~ You're smooth as ever, Dandan!" Mustard laughed heartily.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"With your strength, you'll probably be ranked number one when the tournament starts, won't you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mm, I should be." Dylan nodded with a trace of regret.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Given his current fame and the fact that he had just absolutely demolished Leon, there was no question\u8212?he'd be seeded number one from the start.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You don't look happy about it though?" Mustard asked, puzzled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Being number one means I won't get to challenge anyone ranked below me. That takes a lot of the fun out of it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan sighed lightly. Honestly, if he were really entering the World Championship, he'd have preferred to fight his way up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Climbing the ranks through battle\u8212?{\i
that} was a sense of fulfillment. Being handed the top spot from the get-go wasn't his style.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mainly, being ranked #1 meant he couldn't initiate challenges. He had all these teams ready, but no chance to give others a taste of the fun. He'd be stuck watching from the sidelines in the early stages while everyone else battled it out. It was unsatisfying.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?" Mustard blinked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But others can still challenge {\i
you}, Dandan."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pfft~ Master, I don't think anyone will be challenging my brother." Lillie giggled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She had traveled extensively with Dylan and met countless powerful trainers. At this point, the only region she hadn't been to was Kalos.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Most Champions across the world already knew of Dylan. With him sitting pretty at the top of the board, who would be crazy enough to go challenge him?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And since he couldn't challenge anyone ranked below him, it meant no matches. It was boring.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Emmm\u8230? can't argue with that. If it were me, I wouldn't challenge Dylan either."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mustard tilted his head and thought for a moment. Fair enough. If they hadn't agreed beforehand that Dylan wouldn't use any of his terrifying Dragon-type legends, Mustard wouldn't have wanted to battle him either.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Leon got obliterated\u8212?what chance did anyone else have?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After dinner, Dylan politely declined Mustard's offer to stay overnight at the dojo. He and the others rode Reshiram toward Hammerlocke City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When they returned, it was already past 8 p.m.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan picked up a fresh batch of Pok\u233?mon from the teleport room at the hotel, courtesy of Professor Rowan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He headed out to the hotel's private training field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come on out."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He opened three Pok\u233? Balls, releasing three Pok\u233?mon before him in a flash of light.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hello there. From today on, I'll be your Trainer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan crouched down, smiling warmly. A gentle wave of Viridian Force flowed out from him, instantly winning the three little ones over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the left was a small, light brown puppy with big blue eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
'Beep~ Rockruff. Rock-type. Puppy Pok\u233?mon.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Inner Focus\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Rock Throw, Double Team, Sand Attack, Tackle, Sucker Punch (Egg Move)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Info: As it matures, its personality becomes more aggressive. Some Trainers abandon it when it becomes too much to handle.'}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's right\u8212?Rockruff. Though not the Own Tempo version Dylan had hoped for.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had been aiming for the special Rockruff with Own Tempo, which could evolve into Dusk Form Lycanroc. But he wasn't too disappointed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No rush. He wasn't planning to build just one Rock-type team. Rowan could keep looking for the right one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Besides, both Midday and Midnight forms were solid with proper training. Dylan wasn't picky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Next, he looked at the one in the middle. A deep gray, metallic body with stubby legs and a large round head. Pale blue eyes\u8212?clearly a little steel beast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
'Beep~ Aron. Steel/Rock-type. Iron Armor Pok\u233?mon.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Heavy Metal\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Rock Tomb, Metal Claw, Harden, Tackle, Draco Meteor (Egg Move)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Info: A troublesome Pok\u233?mon. It eats iron ore to build its steel body, but sometimes chews on bridges or train tracks.'}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nice. A Heavy Metal Aron. Once it evolved into Aggron, it could dish out brutal Heavy Slams.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan nodded in approval. He'd need to stock up on iron ore to feed this one. The more it ate, the better it'd grow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And lastly, the Pok\u233?mon on the far right looked... bizarre. Just a dark blue chunk of rock with two little feet and a hexagonal hole in the center. But that hole wasn't its eye\u8212?it was its ear.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
'Beep~ Roggenrola. Rock-type. Mantle Pok\u233?mon.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Weak Armor\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Stealth Rock, Harden, Sand Attack, Tackle, Gravity (Egg Move)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Info: It reacts to sound. Its core emits heat, making it warm to the touch.'}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Roggenrola with Weak Armor, which would eventually evolve into a Gigalith with Sand Stream.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If he was building a Rock-type team, then Sand Stream was essential\u8212?even though his Tyranitar already had the ability.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But T-tar was the ace\u8212?he couldn't always be the lead. Having Gigalith around gave him options.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, Dylan already had quite a few Rock-types.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iron Thorns, Iron Treads, Nihilego, Stonjourner, Tyranitar, Regirock\u8212?that was already six.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Pok\u233?mon like Regirock were too strong for standard challengers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The same went for most of his other teams. Most Pok\u233?mon had dual-types, so overlapping types were inevitable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like his Fairy-types. Dylan hadn't even tried to build a Fairy team, but he already could.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gardevoir, Whimsicott, Sylveon, Mimikyu, Hatterene, Grimmsnarl\u8212?that was six already. Plus Scream Tail, Flutter Mane, Iron Valiant, and Enamorus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It just worked out that way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just then, Dylan's phone rang.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hello? Chairman? What's wrong?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Chairman Damalanthi.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, it's bad."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lance attacked earlier today!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What?" Dylan was stunned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Senior Lance already made his move? That was fast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This afternoon, Lance struck Mahogany Town in Johto. Reports say Team Rocket had been gathering there."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Slowpoke Well was destroyed in the process, and Dragonair's attacks harmed some innocent civilians. They're being treated now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, he's going too far."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Damalanthi sighed heavily. He knew Lance wouldn't stop after leaving the League, but he didn't think he'd act so quickly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm worried he might go after Vermilion and Fuchsia Gyms next."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Because the Gym Leaders there were Surge and Koga.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Damalanthi believed they had reformed, but Lance probably wouldn't care.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All he'd care about was that they were once Rocket executives.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Damalanthi genuinely feared Lance might go so far as to attack entire cities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I understand. I'll return as soon as possible," Dylan replied after a moment's thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He agreed\u8212?Lance probably wouldn't spare Surge or Koga.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan... You're the only one who can stop him."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Damalanthi let out a long breath. He didn't want to see Lance descend further into darkness.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll do my best to wake him up." Dylan nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After hanging up, he remained silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance was an extremist\u8212?almost to the point of madness. In {\i
Adventures}, he had to be {\i
defeated} to snap out of it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For someone like that, only a crushing defeat could make him reflect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Dylan didn't believe that defeating Lance himself would be enough to change him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their relationship was\u8230? complicated. Even if Dylan won, it wouldn't force Lance to reflect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if he didn't step in, even Giovanni and the others probably couldn't stop a Zekrom-wielding Lance\u8212?let alone if he brought out a Lugia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Giovanni wasn't going to summon Mewtwo to fight. That would only provoke Lance further.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
An idea formed in Dylan's mind. He knew what needed to be done.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
It was time to return to Kanto and deal with Senior Lance.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
(End of Chapter)}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
