381: Chapter 381: Should N Just Flip the Table?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before coming to Kanto, N had genuinely imagined what his battle with Dylan would be like.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, this was a clash between the "Hero of Truth" and the "Hero of Ideals"\u8212?a battle foretold for a thousand years!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The very embodiment of the Dragon Gods, coming to blows!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, N was well aware of the vast gap between himself and Dylan. Dylan was simply too powerful. N had even seen the battle where Dylan utterly shut out Leon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And even if Dylan chose to use his legendary Pok\u233?mon in this battle, N felt he could accept that. He just wanted to fulfill this long-awaited "fated" duel.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And to his surprise, Dylan hadn't used any overpowering legendaries to steamroll him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In fact, Dylan had shown what you might call\u8230? restraint.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now, N wasn't sure how to describe that "restraint."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had come seeking Dylan's true self\u8212?but this "truth" was\u8230? a little too real.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thanks for your hard work\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
N muttered quietly as he recalled the fainted Archeops. He glanced down at the Pok\u233? Ball in his hand, his eyes dimming.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He could feel it\u8212?Archeops's bewilderment and frustration. That vile, underhanded, sinister black-skinned lizard had cheated it!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If it had been a straight fight, Bird Boss would've smoked that thing!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that sleazy Salazzle had played dead and sneak-attacked it. Despicable!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You did great. Rest well now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the other side, Dylan recalled his battered Salazzle and praised her with a gentle smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then he casually pulled out another Pok\u233? Ball and looked up at N.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Looks like you've been a bit too careless, N. If you're not more cautious, this battle won't end well for you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He toyed with the Pok\u233? Ball in his hand, voice low and deliberate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
N: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alder: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not just N\u8212?even the spectators went silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like\u8230? was that supposed to be a pep talk?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?I understand."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
N took a deep breath, trying to adjust to Dylan's peculiar battle style.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd realized it now\u8212?Dylan didn't fight like any other trainer he'd ever faced. Dylan's style was just\u8230? something else.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright then. My third Pok\u233?mon will be\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan gave a small nod and tossed out his next Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Arbok! Time to battle!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A flash of light, and a massive, muscular purple cobra rose from the ground, flicking its tongue and locking its cold, menacing eyes on N.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Arbok!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wow, it's been ages since I've seen this Arbok fight." Ilene smiled with a touch of nostalgia, her thoughts drifting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This Arbok had been one of Dylan's original Poison-type powerhouses. She'd even been there the day he caught it at Mt. Moon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With time, Arbok's strength had grown rapidly. Eventually, it became too strong to use against average Gym challengers\u8212?unless they were particularly elite, Dylan couldn't justify sending it out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And as Dylan began training teams of various types, Arbok saw less and less screen time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But its power only continued to grow. Its size, too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Last she remembered, Arbok had already grown over four meters\u8212?well above the species' average. Now it looked close to five meters, with a body thick enough to swallow a full-grown human whole.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A truly terrifying sight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet, Ilene and Lillie weren't afraid at all. They were used to Dylan's Pok\u233?mon by now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Over time, even this cold, brooding Arbok had become a familiar face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Arbok, huh\u8230?" N muttered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arbok was a pure Poison-type. But it could learn all sorts of moves, especially a wide array of biting attacks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
N's gaze flicked to the ground. His brows furrowed slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had originally planned to have Archeops clear the Toxic Spikes after dealing with Salazzle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now that Archeops was down\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
