{\qc
387: Chapter 387: What\u8217?s So Pretty and Charming?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That Diantha actually wanted to challenge him\u8212?Dylan was honestly a little surprised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Since it's a request from Miss Diantha, I'd be happy to accept."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan naturally agreed. To battle Diantha was something he couldn't ask for more.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was genuinely interested in powerful trainers from the original works.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you very much."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha gave a soft, elegant smile\u8212?it was quite radiant.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then Miss Diantha, according to the rules of the Rota Gym, you'll draw an attribute first."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie took a small spinning wheel from her bag and handed it to Diantha.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"All right."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha curiously examined the little spinner. Dylan was a multi-type trainer and was gradually working toward mastering all types.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was no secret anymore. Some people, frankly, made the gap between them and others feel inhuman.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha pressed the "Go" button, and the pointer began spinning rapidly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before long, it slowed and finally stopped in a pink section.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fairy type, huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha looked at the indicator, her clear eyes sparkling slightly. She was hardly unfamiliar with Fairy types.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everyone knew her ace was Gardevoir, which was part Fairy-type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Shall we find a battlefield nearby?" Dylan asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come with me. I know a proper battlefield nearby."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a former Kalos Champion, Diantha knew Lumiose City like the back of her hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She sent Serena a message and then led Dylan's group to a large nearby training facility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This facility was well-equipped\u8212?even with a scoreboard. Not bad.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There were still a few trainers sparsely training there. Dylan and Diantha took up opposite sides of the battlefield and looked across at each other.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The scoreboard lit up, displaying half-body portraits of Dylan and Diantha.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then I, Leaf, will be the referee!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaf confidently walked to the center of the field and glanced at both Dylan and Diantha.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now beginning the Rota Gym challenge match. Challenger: Diantha."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Battle rules: 6-vs-6 full battle. Gym Leader Dylan sends out first and cannot switch Pok\u233?mon. If all six of Dylan's Pok\u233?mon are defeated, the challenge is successful."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Battle start!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaf swung her arm down and then stepped off the field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All the commotion quickly attracted the attention of nearby trainers. After all, Pok\u233?mon battles were hugely popular, and a public full battle was a big deal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Whoa! That really is Miss Diantha\u8212?I thought she looked familiar!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"She's having a full battle? Wait, the guy she's battling\u8230? he looks really familiar too!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Damn! That's Dylan, the Champion of Kanto! I saw his match against Galar's Champion Leon!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's Diantha doing?! She's battling that kind of monster?! Nooo, not my goddess Diantha!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Can you shut up? Miss Diantha is way stronger than that clown Leon. No way she gets steamrolled like him!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Spectators quickly gathered. Diantha wasn't just a former Kalos Champion\u8212?she was also a mega-celebrity, beloved by fans and trainers alike.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even though she wasn't Champion anymore, it didn't affect her popularity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Kalos trainers firmly believed Diantha was as strong\u8212?or stronger\u8212?than any other region's Champion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Naturally. Who'd admit their own Champion was worse?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Looks like we've drawn quite a crowd, Champion Dylan..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha looked a bit sheepish as she noticed the growing audience. Her popularity in Kalos was truly sky-high.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No need to worry. I'm used to having spectators when accepting gym challenges." Dylan smiled and shook his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then let's begin in earnest, Miss Diantha."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan slowly unfastened the top two buttons of his black shirt, loosening his collar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Since this is your first challenge at my Rota Gym, please allow me to formally introduce myself."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I am Dylan, Gym Leader of the Rota Gym\u8212?a multi-type trainer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing Dylan's calm and composed tone, Diantha's eyes gleamed slightly. As expected of Champion Dylan\u8212?what an opening.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Today, I'll be using Fairy-type Pok\u233?mon to battle you. Miss Diantha, you're not unfamiliar with Fairy-types, are you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They are graceful and elegant, as enchanting as fairies, and behind their cute exteriors lies tremendous power."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan slowly slipped on his black gloves and enlarged a Pok\u233? Ball in his hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Are you ready, Miss Diantha? Then allow me to show you the unique charm of Fairy-types."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With eyes locked on Diantha, Dylan tossed his first Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"My first Pok\u233?mon will be\u8212?this one!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Klefki, ready for battle!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233? Ball opened with a flash of white light, revealing a floating Pok\u233?mon that looked exactly like a keyring, with various keys dangling from it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Klefki.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beep~ Klefki, Steel/Fairy-type. The Key Ring Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Prankster\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Play Rough, Imprison, Fairy Lock, Torment, Reflect, Light Screen, Spikes...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: It never lets go of keys it likes. To prevent theft, it often carries the keys to vaults.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Klefki as the opener, huh? That little guy is no joke."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaf clicked her tongue as she listened to the Rotom Dex. She hadn't seen Dylan use Klefki before, but it was clearly annoying to deal with.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That much was obvious. With the Prankster ability and a Steel/Fairy typing, Klefki had amazing resistances.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Immune to Dragon and Poison, and only weak to Fire and Ground\u8212?easily one of the best type combinations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hawlucha, you're up."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a brief pause, Diantha tossed her first Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Pok\u233?mon with humanoid and avian features landed in front of her. It had beautiful, colorful plumage, a beak-like head, and a powerful build.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Hawlucha.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beep~ Hawlucha, Fighting/Flying-type. The Wrestling Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Unburden\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Sky Attack, Reckless, High Jump Kick, Flying Press, Swords Dance, Detect, Roost...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Description: It leaps gracefully with its wings, delivering elegant but deadly strikes. These moves are honed in its forest home.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looks pretty strong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie curiously observed the muscular Hawlucha\u8212?it looked just like a gladiator.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Hawlucha is weak to Fairy. That means Diantha chose a Pok\u233?mon with a disadvantage from the start.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She sure is confident.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Challenger moves first," Dylan said with gentlemanly grace, motioning with his hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then I won't hold back." Diantha lifted her arm elegantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hawlucha, Swords Dance!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha went for a buff first. Swords Dance boosts physical attack by two stages, making Hawlucha a lot more dangerous.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hawlucha struck a strong pose, and an intense, sharp aura surged around it\u8212?Swords Dance!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fairy Lock."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan calmly issued his command.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Klefki swayed slightly, pink energy flying toward Hawlucha and forming a pink lock symbol that attached to it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha's brow furrowed. She recognized the move\u8212?Fairy Lock! Klefki's signature.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It's like Mean Look: it prevents switching out for all non-Ghost Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But unlike Mean Look, Fairy Lock has a time limit\u8212?and a stronger binding effect. You can't escape even with Baton Pass.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Prankster active, Fairy Lock activated instantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Spikes," Dylan ordered again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Klefki continued jingling as sharp spike fragments scattered across the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just as the Spikes were laid, Hawlucha finished its Swords Dance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hawlucha, go in with Fire Punch!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha's expression turned serious. Her Hawlucha had inherited Defog, but she didn't want to risk Klefki pulling something during the setup.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although Hawlucha prefers fighting on the ground, it could fly\u8212?so as long as it didn't land, the Spikes wouldn't matter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hawlucha bent its knees, leapt high, and spread its wings to glide toward Klefki.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its flight was like a glide\u8212?fast and stylish\u8212?closing the distance in no time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flames erupted from its right fist\u8212?Fire Punch!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Metal Sound." Dylan smiled coolly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
WNNG~ WNNG~!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Klefki backed off, shaking violently as unbearable metallic screeches turned into semi-solid sound waves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hawlucha flinched, as though struck\u8212?Metal Sound tore into its eardrums, contorting its expression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
White light flashed around it\u8212?its Special Defense fell sharply.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hang in there, Hawlucha!" Diantha's face tightened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Prankster made Klefki's status moves lightning-fast\u8212?there was no time to prepare.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Metal Sound didn't deal damage, but it was grating.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Hawlucha was one of Diantha's main Pok\u233?mon. It quickly adapted and resumed its charge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But its speed clearly dropped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hawlucha threw its flaming fist\u8212?but Klefki narrowly dodged with a sideways juke.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Hawlucha's experience showed\u8212?it followed up with a left-hand Fire Punch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thunder Wave."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Electric sparks crackled around Klefki and shot straight into Hawlucha.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Paralysis!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Electric current surged through Hawlucha, freezing its muscles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It lost its balance and fell toward the ground\u8212?crashing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Diantha's expression visibly changed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What a nasty little thing!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What's so cute and charming about your Fairy-type Pok\u233?mon?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
(End of Chapter)}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
