"Seriously?" Leaf asked, raising an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's true! Hoopa used to be super strong!" Hoopa puffed up its little chest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaf and Lillie both looked at Dylan. They knew he'd know whether it was true or not.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well\u8230? Hoopa really did cause a major incident long ago. Just how strong it was\u8212?I'm not entirely sure."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meray's eyes sparkled. From what she and Baraz knew, Hoopa had been brought to the Valley of Creation by their great-grandfather, Ghris, after wreaking havoc. Ghris had sealed Hoopa's power as punishment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hoopa's power was definitely immense."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan gently pinched Hoopa's cheek as he explained:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A hundred years ago, Desert City was just a poor, remote town. Hoopa arrived in its Unbound Form."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It took some of the villagers' food and repaid them with vast wealth. Thanks to Hoopa's generosity, the town flourished, and the people adored Hoopa."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing this, Hoopa puffed up its chest with pride.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Life improved, and people began to seek entertainment. Eventually, they asked Hoopa to show its power by battling other Pok\u233?mon."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Being the show-off it was, Hoopa agreed. It defeated many powerful Pok\u233?mon, and the more it fought, the more it got carried away."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Using its dimensional rings, Hoopa began summoning legendary Pok\u233?mon and defeating them\u8212?just to prove how strong it was."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan scratched Hoopa's chin fondly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was Hoopa in a nutshell\u8212?immensely powerful, but obsessed with attention and admiration. That desire for recognition defined both Hoopa Confined and Unbound.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Reshiram, Zekrom, Regigigas, Kyogre, Groudon\u8230? Hoopa beat all of them. And it wasn't even 1v1."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But all that fighting brought destruction to the town. That was the disaster Hoopa caused."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eventually, a traveler named Ghris confronted Hoopa and sealed away its powers."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan told the story calmly. Hoopa scratched its head sheepishly\u8212?not exactly regretful, but clearly a little embarrassed after a hundred years of reflection.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You were really that strong, huh?" Leaf stared in awe at the small Pok\u233?mon before her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hehe~ Hoopa is amazing!" Hoopa grinned from ear to ear.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But something's bothering me\u8230? if Hoopa was that strong, how could a human seal it?" Ilene asked curiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's not so strange. Ghris was a follower of Arceus\u8212?the creator. He may have actually received Arceus's blessing."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan shook his head. In the Pok\u233?mon world, humans could wield many kinds of power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the strongest of them all likely came from the lineage of the Valley of Creation\u8212?those who worshiped Arceus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The movie never explained Ghris's origins, but the valley housed a statue of Arceus. That made their faith clear.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Arceus\u8230??"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The girls blinked. They'd never heard of that one\u8212?but clearly, it was an immensely powerful Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Miss Meray, you're aware of this, aren't you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes. My family has always worshipped Arceus. Ghris was my great-grandfather\u8230? but Mr. Dylan, how do you know all this?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meray stared at him in astonishment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I like to study regional legends and histories. Just a hobby."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?I see. You're very knowledgeable," she said, still confused but choosing not to press further.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then is there really no way for Hoopa to return to its original form?" Lillie asked curiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nope. My power's all sealed. I need to get it back first."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hoopa's voice dropped as it pouted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ghris said I had to understand the meaning of 'punishment.' But I still don't get it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It scratched its head in frustration. The concept of "atonement" was beyond its mischievous mind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, after a hundred years in the valley, Hoopa had grown used to life without power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Great-grandfather did it for your own good. You were out of control."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meray sighed and ruffled Hoopa's head affectionately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmmph~" Hoopa crossed its arms and looked away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Honestly, I think Hoopa's matured a lot. Even if it got its powers back, I doubt it'd go wild again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan smiled. If the shadow Hoopa didn't interfere, Hoopa Confined would never lose control again\u8212?not with Meray and Baraz by its side.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"True. My brother and I have been considering it. But we'll need time to locate the Prison Bottle."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meray gently patted Hoopa's belly, looking down at it with soft eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
