{\qc
424: Chapter 424: Who Dares Challenge Kanto\u8217?s Elite Four?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Let's see how many Pok\u233?mon Raihan can take down from Giovanni's team?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Dylan said this, Leon, Steven, and Cynthia were briefly stunned. What did he mean by that?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't hard to understand\u8212?but the implication was\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Uncle Giovanni is really strong. Super impressive, actually. Before big brother came along, the only one in Kanto who could rival Champion Lance was Uncle Giovanni."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lillie smiled sweetly, her tone full of pride.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all\u8230? Kanto was her home now!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"He's that strong?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wallace was surprised. He hadn't heard much about Giovanni before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raihan, ranked No. 14 on the Ultra Ball leaderboard, was now officially challenging Giovanni, ranked No. 13.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While this battle didn't have the same global attention as yesterday's clash between Leon and Iris, it was still a high-profile match.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One was the "Storm of Dragons" from Galar, said to be Champion-tier in any other region. The other was the most formidable member of Kanto's Elite Four\u8212?naturally, the match drew attention.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Plus, the Indigo Plateau arena now supported Dynamax energy zones, meaning Raihan could use his signature strategy too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Worth noting: In the Sword/Shield games, Raihan's ace\u8212?Duraludon\u8212?didn't have an evolution. But in the Scarlet/Violet DLC, Duraludon gained an evolved form: Archaludon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In this world, Raihan had naturally chosen to evolve his Duraludon into Archaludon, since it was much stronger in battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This meant losing access to Gigantamax Duraludon\u8212?but honestly, Dylan thought that was a good thing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, who in their right mind would use Gigantamax Duraludon? That thing was so janky even a stray dog wouldn't touch it\u8212?except Raihan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni sent out his lead: Great Tusk, a powerhouse Dylan had gifted him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni truly loved this Pok\u233?mon. He'd initially considered raising an Iron Treads, but after bonding with Great Tusk, he never looked back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From any angle, Great Tusk was outstanding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had already been powerful when Dylan gave it to him, and now it had become a core part of Giovanni's main team.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raihan, seeing Great Tusk, froze mid-throw with Coalossal's Pok\u233? Ball in hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Paradox Pok\u233?mon and Ultra Beasts were well-known in Trainer circles by now, and Paradox Pok\u233?mon had two possible Abilities:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For past forms, Protosynthesis; for future forms, Quark Drive. The former was boosted by sun, the latter by Electric Terrain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Great Tusk? You could tell from its design it was clearly a past form.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Raihan may be called the 'Storm of Dragons,' but in truth, his real strength is in weather teams\u8212?he's trained extensively to win in any environment."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Raihan silently withdraw his Pok\u233? Ball, Dylan chuckled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's right\u8212?despite his title, Raihan was more of a weather master. His team even included two different weather setters. Crazy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, Raihan had been planning to open with Coalossal's Drought ability and set up harsh sunlight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that would've directly boosted Great Tusk via Protosynthesis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So he had no choice but to put Coalossal away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You sure know Raihan well," Leon noted in surprise. "You're right\u8212?he definitely wanted to open with Drought. But using it against Great Tusk would've been a huge disadvantage."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon understood Raihan\u8212?after all, they'd battled ten times. He knew him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Big brother's great at weather teams too, but why doesn't he use Dragonair like Champion Lance?" Lillie asked curiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair was one of the best weather setters among Dragons\u8212?it could freely shift the climate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's not the same, Lillie. Not everyone can train a Dragonair to the level Lance has."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven shook his head. He still remembered the Goldenrod battle, where Lance's two Dragonair displayed incredible strength.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was genuinely impressed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly. Most Dragon-type Pok\u233?mon only reach their full potential in their final evolution\u8212?especially late bloomers like Dragonite."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia nodded in agreement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"While Dragonair does have the rare ability to control weather, its base stats aren't all that impressive. Sure, there are exceptions who can raise it to great heights\u8212?but it takes tremendous effort."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Compared to that, using other Pok\u233?mon with built-in weather abilities is just\u8230? more efficient."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini were rare, but Raihan certainly had the resources to get one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, why bother?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair's weather control was nice, but was it worth dedicating a main team slot? That was debatable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And training a Dragonair to be as strong as a Dragonite? Not exactly easy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's why most Trainers prefer high base stat Pok\u233?mon\u8212?stronger stats = higher natural ceiling, and with training, they get even stronger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I see\u8230?" Lillie nodded thoughtfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, the battle had begun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raihan led with Sandaconda, a Ground-type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His other weather setter was Gigalith, but Great Tusk resisted Rock moves. And Sandstorm\u8230? wouldn't help much here.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That Sandaconda looks\u8230? weird," Lillie murmured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was basically a huge sand snake, coiled into a spiral\u8212?hence the name.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Beep\u8212?Sandaconda, Ground-type. Sand Snake Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ability: Sand Spit\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moves: Sand Tomb, Coil, Slam, Dig, Glare, Stomping Tantrum\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dex Entry: It coils its body in this unique way to maximize the efficiency of sand it ejects from its sand sacs."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It looked powerful. Lillie stared at the Rotomdex description, wondering how it would perform in battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The match began.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni may be known as the "Earthshaker," and people might think of Earth-type strategies as "solid," "defensive," and "unshakable."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And while his tactics were indeed steady\u8212?he was no slouch when it came to offense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Great Tusk was a brute.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It charged in with Rapid Spin, closing distance fast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then\u8212?BAM! A head-on clash of High Horsepower versus High Horsepower!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Great Tusk launched Sandaconda off the field with sheer force, shocking Raihan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The difference in power was obvious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then Great Tusk spun rapidly\u8212?Ice Shard glinting in the air as it formed a freezing Rapid Spin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two ice-coated attacks crashed into Sandaconda.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sandaconda collapsed. Easy win.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"WOOOO!!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Told you! Who dares challenge Kanto's Elite Four?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Giovanni, you're amazing! That was clean!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That Great Tusk is gorgeous\u8212?I'm drooling, bros!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Storm of Dragons? Champion in another region? Sorry, this region's built different!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Giovanni OP!!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The chat was going wild with Kanto fans.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe they were nervous before the match\u8212?but now?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni gave them confidence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From that first clash, it was clear the strength gap wasn't small.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Impressive\u8230? looks like Raihan's in for a rough day."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
