Though he wouldn't openly admit it, Giovanni was well aware of the pride swelling inside him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Having thousands scream his name in admiration and awe\u8230? it was a kind of thrill and satisfaction he'd never felt during his time in Team Rocket.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, in a shaded corner of the stadium, three figures watched the scene with complicated expressions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If Archer and the others knew the boss is now a national idol\u8230? what kind of face do you think they'd make?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge's rough face twisted into something unreadable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Koga: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina: (\u8212?)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They'd probably think I'd gone nuts," Surge scratched his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, this felt like a dream. He'd once felt pretty guilty\u8212?after all, he had been talked into returning as Vermilion City's Gym Leader by Jenny, turning over a new leaf.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it was only after that that Surge learned\u8230? the boss himself had already been "recruited" by the Kanto League!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What kind of twist was that?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since then, Surge hadn't contacted Giovanni in a long time. He genuinely didn't know how to face him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He hadn't spoken to Koga or Sabrina either, despite them all being former Rocket executives.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though they'd been re-added to the "Gym Leader Group Chat," Surge hadn't said a word in there since. Once a "problematic figure," he kept his head down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Officer Jenny's idea for the Gym Leaders to come watch Raihan's challenge match\u8212?treat it like a day off.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And so, the three former Rocket executives were together again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No matter where they stood now, they shared a common past.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So we were in prison for nothing\u8230? I ate jail food for months," Surge grumbled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Koga: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't lump me in with you two. I've always been the Saffron Gym Leader," Sabrina said coldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"???"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge and Koga blinked at her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Problem?" Sabrina gave them a cool glance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oh. So just because she didn't get exposed and didn't serve time, she's suddenly clean and above them, huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge and Koga exchanged a glance and fell silent. Technically\u8230? yeah, she wasn't wrong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Either way, we're all starting over," Koga finally said in a low voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There's no boss anymore. I'm not a Rocket exec now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Having returned to the Fuchsia Gym, Koga had realized\u8212?he preferred being a clean, normal person. He didn't want anything to do with evil organizations anymore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He still had a younger sister. A daughter. He wasn't alone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I mean, this World Championship thing is pretty nice," Surge grinned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sabrina, I heard you applied to train in Unova? What's that about?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though they weren't exactly close as colleagues, their relationship wasn't bad either.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina frowned slightly, a rare expression of hesitation crossing her face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
