{\qc
427: Chapter 427: Dylan\u8217?s Complete Trio\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Scattering hazards and then forcing the opponent to switch with Whirlwind or Roar\u8212?this was one of the most enduring tactics Dylan remembered from his past life in the Pok\u233?mon games.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A very nasty strategy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But in reality, pulling it off effectively wasn't so simple.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It all came down to the hazards.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the games, moves were restricted\u8212?each Pok\u233?mon only had four slots. That meant very few trainers actually carried Defog, Rapid Spin, or similar hazard-clearing moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unless it was during a meta where "stall" was everywhere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the real world was different. Here, there were no limits to the number of moves a Pok\u233?mon could learn\u8212?if it could be taught, it could be used.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So unless you caught your opponent completely off guard, using hazards to dominate a full battle was unrealistic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, if you could make them matter even for a short while in a six-on-six, that was already a success.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Going to use Roar?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven's brows furrowed as he quickly ran through his options.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Skarmory could inherit Whirlwind and learn Roar via TM\u8212?forcing a switch wasn't the problem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The real question was, which legendaries did Dylan bring?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If they were anything like the myths, dragging out a "big daddy" could be a disaster.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven had heard of a trainer who got "lucky" once\u8212?Roar pulled out both Reshiram and Kyurem in the same match\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The very thought of that made his scalp go numb.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?Forget it. Too risky."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His train of thought halted. Mature and steady as always, Steven wasn't the type to gamble against the unknown.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Besides\u8230? he'd just drawn his own golden legendary not long ago. He still didn't know if that made him fortunate or cursed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come back, Skarmory."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven recalled his armored bird. No point letting it keep trading with Galarian Zapdos\u8212?Taunt had already locked Skarmory into only attacking moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And in raw offense, Skarmory simply couldn't match Zapdos.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Claydol!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He tossed out his second Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
White light flashed, and a dark-bodied creature with rings of eyes floated before him\u8212?his trusty Claydol.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
