Ice-type Icy Wind! And as a Ground/Dragon, Mega Garchomp was four times weak to Ice!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet Garchomp didn't even blink. With a savage swing, it cleaved the icy gale apart, the frost blasting harmlessly past on either side.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A single force breaking all technique\u8212?this Garchomp is brutal!" Mei stuck out her tongue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But it still can't hit Flutter Mane. Flutter Mane's too agile." Toko shook her head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not necessarily, Toko." Mei grinned mischievously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Toko froze, then quickly realized\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Stealth Rocks. Cynthia's waiting for the opening."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mega Garchomp's relentless pursuit suddenly made sense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But wasn't it strange? If Flutter Mane couldn't deal with Mega Garchomp, why didn't Dylan just switch it out?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And then it happened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flutter Mane, backing away to dodge, finally stumbled into a solid mass\u8212?Stealth Rock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Boom!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Flutter Mane." Dylan called calmly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The stones detonated, blasting Flutter Mane backward in pain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But its eyes glowed with an eerie black light\u8212?unseen to the others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Something's not right\u8230?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia frowned. It was too easy. Was Dylan\u8230? handing her the win?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He could've switched Flutter Mane out. This wasn't a Gym match.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And surely he hadn't forgotten about Stealth Rocks?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Flutter Mane forced back, one Shadow Claw from Mega Garchomp would finish it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Already injured by Porygon2 earlier, Flutter Mane couldn't possibly take that hit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan couldn't not know this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garchomp! Shadow Claw!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The thought flashed in Cynthia's mind, but the opening was too good. Instinctively, she gave the command.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mega Garchomp's scythe gleamed with ghostly light, slicing down toward the staggered Flutter Mane.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, escape was impossible.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But then\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait! Garchomp!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia's eyes widened. She shouted just in time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mega Garchomp froze, its scythe jerking off-course, barely missing Flutter Mane's head. The Shadow Claw's wind whipped through its ghostly mane.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flutter Mane's wicked grin stiffened. The black glow in its eyes flickered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Seriously? That close\u8212?and you missed?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If I'd known, I would've thrown myself into it!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flutter Mane felt like it had just lost a fortune. To drag Garchomp down with Destiny Bond would've been so satisfying!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You held back?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The smile on Dylan's face faltered, his brow arching.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes\u8212?if that Shadow Claw had struck, Flutter Mane would've gone down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the moment it hit the Stealth Rocks, it had already triggered Destiny Bond, ready to take Mega Garchomp with it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cynthia, looks like you figured it out."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
