In this world, unlike the games, even a Gigantamax Pok\u233?mon could choose whether to use standard Max Moves or their exclusive G-Max moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Naturally, Leon went for G-Max Fireball!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven immediately recalled Metagross and sent out his fifth Pok\u233?mon\u8212?Aggron.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rock resisted Fire, though Steel was weak to it, so Aggron wasn't entirely doomed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dodging a G-Max move was nearly impossible anyway. Steven didn't even try.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He ordered Aggron to strike back with Stone Edge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under the burning sunlight brought on by G-Max Fireball's effect, Fire-type moves became even stronger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon followed up with Max Knuckle, a Fighting-type move\u8212?super effective against Aggron's quadruple weakness!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven wisely used Protect, blocking most of the damage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even so, the sheer force of Max Knuckle broke through, dealing massive harm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Another Max Knuckle followed. Aggron, battered and desperate, launched a final Stone Edge head-on.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't enough. Aggron fell, and though Gigantamax ended, Cinderace was badly hurt too\u8212?Stone Edge had done serious damage, even against its doubled HP.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven brought back Metagross. After a grueling clash, both Pok\u233?mon went down together.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven now had only two Pok\u233?mon left.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon's third Pok\u233?mon, Inteleon, made quick work of Skarmory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then Steven's ace\u8212?his shiny Metagross\u8212?entered the field and Mega Evolved.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A heated showdown with Inteleon followed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
