488: Chapter 489: Arceus, What Do You Want, Dylan?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Since that's the case, things will be easier."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Having finally persuaded Arceus, Dylan nodded in satisfaction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the end, power still spoke the loudest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If they hadn't first ganged up on Arceus and beaten it into submission, there was no way the vengeful god would be this cooperative. That would've been a dream.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But after that beating, things were different. {\i
I've already proven I'm stronger than you\u8212?why would I need to deceive you? What good would that do me?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dialga."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan turned to Origin Dialga. To travel through time, of course they'd need its power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Dialga of this world was still lying on the ground half-dead. Arceus had hit it hard\u8212?just like in the movie, when it had been shot down after barely a few moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That last bit of strength had been used to send Ash and his friends through time. After that, it had collapsed completely. Some even wondered if it was already done for.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even now, though it hadn't joined the last battle, Dialga hadn't recovered despite resting for a while.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan recalled Eternatus and the others, not at all worried that Arceus might strike while his back was turned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though Arceus still harbored resentment, it was, after all, the Creator. It wouldn't stoop to betrayal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait for me here. I won't be long."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
