Arceus lifted its head slightly, its crimson-tinged eyes filled with indescribable emotion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course it remembered\u8212?too well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This was the day of your promised eclipse. Let's go see for ourselves what Damos is doing now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan released the shining Mewtwo from its Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus nodded, though a swirl of emotion churned in its heart\u8212?hatred, but also tension.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What if Dylan was telling the truth?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had seen Damos's betrayal with its own eyes, yes\u8212?but what if? What if what it saw hadn't been real? What if it had misunderstood?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If that were true\u8230? maybe it would bring it peace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus's emotions were tangled and uncertain. It didn't even know what kind of "truth" it was hoping for anymore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With the shining Mewtwo's psychic power, the two entered the temple boldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though they encountered many guards along the way, Mewtwo needed only a glance to hypnotize them, letting them pass unimpeded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At this point in the timeline, Arceus had yet to arrive. Dylan and Arceus made their way into the inner chambers of the temple.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Along the way, they saw the Pok\u233?mon prepared in advance\u8212?the ones meant to ambush Arceus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing this, Arceus's eyes grew bloodier, its aura flaring in rage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Calm yourself," Dylan said gently. "Trust me\u8212?and trust in your bond with Damos. You chose him for a reason, didn't you? Because you saw the goodness in his heart."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I was wrong," Arceus replied in a low voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No. You weren't. Look for yourself."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
