"And as you already know, what followed was tragedy. But through it all, Damos never betrayed you. Yes, humans are flawed and greedy\u8212?but the one you trusted, Damos, never was."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan's voice was calm but heavy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was human greed\u8212?Marcus's greed\u8212?that had caused all this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And we've always respected you, Arceus. Please believe that, even if some humans are vile, not all of us are beyond redemption."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus trembled. Dylan's words echoed in its mind as it stared at Damos. Memories surged back\u8212?of trust, of faith, of betrayal that might not have been betrayal at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time passed in silence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At last, Arceus slowly closed its eyes. When they opened again, the red glow was gone\u8212?replaced by clear, gentle light.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So that's how it was\u8230?" came its ancient, weary thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It felt sorrow\u8212?both for Damos and for itself, trapped in hatred for a thousand years.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had hated Damos so deeply because it had trusted him so completely\u8212?entrusting him with five of its Plates, turned into the Jewel of Life, to fill this land with vitality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And that trust, it believed, had been betrayed. That was the true source of its wrath.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus was the Creator, the Divine One of Sinnoh, the God of the Beginning. But it, too, had the heart of a sentient being\u8212?capable of anger, grief, and despair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No one could give their heart in trust and remain unmoved when that trust was shattered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you, Dylan. If not for you\u8230? I might have made an unforgivable mistake."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus turned its calm gaze on him. The hostility was gone, replaced by peace and divine grace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the Arceus before had been a vengeful god of wrath, now it was once more the benevolent guardian spoken of in legend.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan smiled. "No need to thank me. I've always deeply respected you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus held his gaze. The respect was genuine\u8212?it could feel that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, the beating earlier had also been {\i
very} real.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even now, it still carried the wounds from Eternatus and the others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
