"And you're fine letting this version of you go through that pain again?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is the flow of time. I must not disturb it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus shook its head. The weight of time was immense. Changing history could cause unpredictable consequences.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is that so?" Dylan tilted his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From what he knew of the movie, history didn't change much even after time travel\u8212?only the future's "results" shifted slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I said before\u8212?if I truly wronged Damos, then I must face punishment," Arceus said calmly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan blinked. {\i
So you're seriously letting your past self suffer again?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
That's pretty hardcore.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dylan, this has been an invaluable lesson for me. I trusted too much in what my eyes saw as truth\u8212?and nearly caused a disaster beyond imagination."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This trial\u8230? was good for me." Arceus seemed to sense Dylan's thoughts and explained softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Haha, as expected of Arceus!" Dylan gave a thumbs-up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only the Creator would be this merciless\u8212?to itself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That said, if I can save Damos, I will. I don't wish to kill the friend I once cherished."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus sighed. In the original history, both Damos and Marcus would have died by its own power\u8212?but that wasn't right.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A moment ago it said it wouldn't change history, and now it wanted to save Damos?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Arceus, you're kind of contradicting yourself here,} Dylan thought silently, though he didn't say it aloud.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under Arceus's will, Damos remained under hypnosis, while the shining Mewtwo erased Marcus's and Bronzong's memories of what had just happened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everything continued along the same path as before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Night fell. The eclipse began.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In this timeline, the other Arceus appeared from the Hall of Origin and descended into the temple\u8212?only to be ambushed without warning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Caught off guard and unguarded toward Damos, it was gravely injured before it could react.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then came rage. The furious god unleashed its might, destroying the temple in an instant before retreating to the Hall of Origin to heal\u8212?carrying a grudge that would last a millennium.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, the current Arceus carried Damos out of the ruins just in time. Damos survived\u8212?the sole witness of that day.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How pitiful. It never imagined its future self would just stand by and watch all this," Dylan said wryly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It {\i
is} me. The future me is still me," Arceus replied with a tired look. "So I will not resent myself\u8212?only be grateful for the truth."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It could tell Dylan was teasing it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"All right, then. Shall we go back? Or do you want to wait until Damos wakes so you can say goodbye?" Dylan asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No need. A trace of memory will suffice."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A soft golden light flowed from Arceus into Damos\u8212?it had left him a memory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go, Dylan. And\u8230? truly, thank you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Any chance that thanks comes with a reward?" Dylan grinned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What do you want?" Arceus asked with a faint smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It truly didn't know how to repay him\u8212?but it was willing to try.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan fell silent, his gaze sweeping up and down the elegant, platinum-white llama before him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Arceus tilted its head slightly. For some reason, Dylan's look made it uneasy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
(End of Chapter)}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
