Boom!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Earth Power erupted violently, torrents of ground energy slamming directly into Hisuian Goodra's shell.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When the attack subsided, Hisuian Goodra emerged from its shell once more.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Shelter complete\u8212?its Defense had risen by two stages.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What a shame. Not the version that boosts evasion."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan thought regretfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Legends: Arceus first released, Hisuian Goodra had once been hailed as the strongest pseudo-legendary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Because of its Steel/Dragon typing\u8212?and because of Shelter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In Legends: Arceus, Shelter didn't just boost defense; it also made Hisuian Goodra much harder to hit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That evasion boost was the real reason it was once considered absurdly overpowered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But by the Scarlet/Violet era, Shelter had been nerfed hard\u8212?essentially becoming a second Iron Defense, boosting Defense by two stages only.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, even so, with its excellent typing, Hisuian Goodra remained extremely formidable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan found it a pity, but it made sense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reality wasn't a game\u8212?numbers couldn't simply translate directly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Shelter boosted evasion in the real world, defining "evasion" itself would be incredibly vague.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Life Dew."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dylan issued another command.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After tanking three Max Quakes and one Earth Power, Hisuian Goodra's condition really wasn't great.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that was fine\u8212?it had recovery.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hisuian Goodra raised its head and sprayed a large amount of water into the air, which scattered and fell as shimmering droplets.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Earth Power!" Selene ordered immediately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dodge," Dylan said calmly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hisuian Goodra wasn't fast, but dodging a single Earth Power wasn't a problem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It quickly moved out of range as Earth Power erupted uselessly into empty ground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, the falling Life Dew sprinkled over Hisuian Goodra, restoring its stamina.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Life Dew's recovery wasn't as strong as Recover, but its advantage was flexibility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Recover required staying still\u8212?meaning guaranteed damage from the opponent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Life Dew didn't.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This won't work."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Selene frowned slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Boosting defenses and healing\u8212?was he worried she'd have Enamorus move in close and use Fighting-type moves?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be honest, she had been thinking about that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, Enamorus's physical attack was also quite good.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now\u8230? was close combat still the right call?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
